{"_id":"0mmuqB8xm7INWn3M","name":"Outdoorsman","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Remove {ranks|setback} from checks to move through terrain or manage environmental effects; reduce overland travel times by 50%."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0nDPPBXClHm3rnXz","name":"Time to Go (Improved)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Spend one Destiny point to perform a move maneuver as an incidental to attempt to move into cover or out of Blast range of a weapon or explosion. One ally at Engaged ranged may all also make a Move maneuver as an incidental."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0uFz51a0nnnRPSzN","name":"Verd Ramos","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Verd Ramos is an older man of about sixty with a quiet, but tired dignity. He is polite and wears a pressed dark green tunic and dark pants. Verd has little information to offer, having never met Oso Maduk or Gustip before. He claims to have been politically exiled from Corellia, and is returning in secret to visit his ill mother."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0wPzAXsQZtCnwqtq","name":"Imperial Dungeoneer","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Imperial dungeoneers are soldiers tasked with overssing the prisoners confined to the Empire’s many dungeon ships, detention facilities, and prison worlds. Despite the sensitive nature of their task, those chosen as guards for the Empire’s enormous population of incarcerated sentients are usually those who couldn’t make the grade in the regular Imperial Army. Considered lowly turnkeys by their compatriots, dungeoneers tend to be bitter and cruel, taking their resentment over thier miserable existence out on their helpless charges."}},"items":[{"_id":"Zw8SD1OivWdpQ6C5","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"zMfabqsGG0vnBXZx","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0x1OyE6b3VxATVYt","name":"Protocol Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The purpose of a protocol droid is to facilitate the interaction of organic beings in a galaxy that has literally thousands upon thousands of unique cultures and civilizations, many of them with conflicting or otherwise exclusive customs and beliefs. Protocol droids were created to prevent offense between different cultures. The advent of the Galactic Empire has lessened the value of protocol droids, since the Empire cares nothing for the culture of its member worlds, but the Alliance has found great use in them to help bridge the gap between the many races that have banded together in hopes of overthrowing the Emperor and his oppressive regime."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0xKD9RTkCraQ5h2F","name":"Planetary Governor","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"In the eyes of the Empire, a planet is the smallest autonomous body of note anywhere within the galaxy. Cities and nations are of no real consequence to a bureaucracy as large as the Empire, but a planet-wide government can at least offer a significant quantity of resources, some extremely valuable, to an extent that makes a planet worthy of attention. For that reason, planetary governors are at least a consideration even to the officers of the Imperial Navy. They are given due consideration and their independence is not trod upon unless absolutely necessary. If planetary considerations stand in the way of the Imperial agenda, however, they are swept aside without a thought; even the most considerate of Imperial officers has his limits."}},"items":[{"_id":"r3JhYv1VGCEq3uu2","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"A9PVKaiPVUjUHpxu","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"QnuxtGUpUnQekFQs","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"7vdj2OLwGSezNToY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0xZj8P2oXKhheeOO","name":"Improved Dodge","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When the character performs the Dodge incidental, the character may make a Move maneuver as an out-of-turn incidental after the triggering attack has been resolved."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0yRzxOAms2kccWhs","name":"Frenzied Attack","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When making a Melee or Brawl check, suffer up to {ranks} Strain to upgrade the attack an equal number of times."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"0ytYXOWOBE8lp4bm","name":"Forsaken Jedi","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Jedi are an ancient order whose light has essentially disappeared from the galaxy. As far as the vast majority of the galaxy is concerned, the Jedi are extinct and their ancient ways were prone to treachery and failure. This is what the Empire has told the people of the galaxy and many believe it. The truth, while not far from the story, is not entirely the same. A handful of Jedi survived the purge that accompanied the birth of the Empire. Most died in subsequent years, but a few remain in hiding. And there are a few whom the Empire never bothered to hunt. Those who fall into this last category are haunted by their failures and by the fact that they are not even enough of a threat to warrant the Empire’s attention. Most have succumbed to self-pity and vice of one form or another If they do not already embrace the dark side, they are not far from doing so."}},"items":[{"_id":"S4GuvcjbB1d5XsvY","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"3Dmqr7SD5j7tjYGf","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"lxaKvGHxBrydD3mq","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"2a7ko5SVCbwHww2K","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"x7sihsHMVIr4TxTd","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"xxrIzJMOOe5LTPSY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
