{"_id":"1EMTx1u7Ft1JUFwk","name":"Galva","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Galva are diminutive and innocuous mammalian species native to Saleucami. They travel in large herds of up to one hundred individuals, feeding off of desert lichens and moss as they migrate across the planet’s oppressively hot equatorial regions. Galva are often hunted for their skins, which can be tanned into a supple leather that has grown increasingly popular (any undamaged hide goes for 1000 credits, rarity 6). As a result, many of the largest galva hers have been depleted by overhunting."}},"items":[{"_id":"nIbVebao2eQCANnD","name":"Teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":2,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"1F15rW46uetciNtp","name":"The Trainer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"nR83OJocgm4TLRrl","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"9fGlTmpDAUtLBg4r","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"X3K6UjlQlvMdqYma","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"I5rA94xG4JMKJQ9M","name":"Skilled Teacher 2","type":"talent","system":{"description":"Before an ally at short range makes a skill check, if that ally has fewer ranks in that skill than the character does, the character may choose to immediately perform a Skilled Teacher incidental to siffer a number of strain, then add an equal number of :success: to the ally’s next check.","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"1Hbvfgnsum8yL3vk","name":"Hondo Ohnaka","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Weequay Hondo Ohnaka, former pirate king of the Ohnaka gang, has fallen far from his glory days during the CLone Wars. His considerable criminal enterprises were destroyed with the ride of the Galactic Empire, leaving Ohnaka operating as a free agent hoping to recover some of his former prestige. Without his sizable fleet and crew of Weequay pirates, Hondo has turned to smuggling, arms dealing and shipjacking to make ends meet. During the rise of the Rebellion, Ohnaka made alliances with everyone from a resistance group on Lothal to Ugnaught information brokers and even the Empire, pledging allegiance and betraying them each in turn in search of profits.\n\nWhite Hondo has gained valuable experiences during his time with pirates, criminals and Rebels, he hasn't changed much. He is still unpredictable, and his plans always take a turn for the chaotic. However, there is something in Hondo’s character that makes a betrayed partner forgive him quickly, and Hondo himself never holds a grudge against an . “old friend”."}},"items":[{"_id":"MOvDBqHKDMF2UXAJ","name":"Modified holdout blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":2,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"xxJX5RiS6VwdhUTY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Iz3H1Qg03xYolTrV","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"YJapLuJRHqz8gtFA","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"iCnKgLVlZAjC3I83","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"1HgKBOBcbPULzkrx","name":"Tibannuck","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Generally looked upon as simple creatures somewhat akin to mynocks, at least one notable sentientologist has presented compelling evidence to suggest that the tibannuck are a sentient race. Although the city’s current Baron Administrator has ended the administrative bounties on tibannuck kills, Imperial law has refused to recognize the creatures as intelligent, and thus several independent sources continue offering bounties on them."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
