{"_id":"4DLJudTe96SSjEMc","name":"Darth Vader","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Many dark tales are told about a black-armoured humanoid who serves as the Emperor’s most trusted enforcer and is perhaps the most feared being in the Empire. Rumoured to live in a forbidding castle on a world of lava, this warrior wields a red lightsaber and possesses terrifying powers that suggest he has a connection to the dreaded Sith. The few who claim to have survived encounters with this individual are unsure whether the armour houses a living being, a combat droid, or even a clone trooper. Many even fear that duplicates could be activated if the first is ever defeated.\n\nIn addition to his other duties to the Empire, Darth Vader is believed to be the most senior member of the Inquisitorius, and legends abound of his pursuit of target after target when other agents failed in their efforts. It is possible that Vader has trained Inquisitors in the techniques required to eliminate Force-sensitive targets."}},"items":[{"_id":"6ExnTeaIKFr7VIpJ","name":"Vader’s Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":1,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder, Superior, Vicious 2, Dual-Phase"}},{"_id":"6Y75ZKYBqI3z3wmw","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Xb1ILsPhIvTGjyX8","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"aqMVSdtVBDU9aeYt","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"NZExfOv9U0MAXHG7","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"5c1XSdibyye3IFAZ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Xb4IYOCvZWXIRWWU","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"r8WAXKG3aZpUFLDA","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"4DZHAg0oSNYQwiQZ","name":"Besalisk Adventurer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A common figure in the cantinas and sabacc dens of the Outer Rim is the wandering Besalisk adventurer. These bulky four-armed avians are known for their generosity, loyalty, and fearless approach to any dangers they might face in their travels. Gregarious, clever, and sharply observant, they can prove to be a valuable source of obscure information. However, many Besalisks hide their own agenda beneath their genial demeanor, and those who interact with them would do well to remember it."}},"items":[{"_id":"K3mLDX18Q5vq9mGY","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"xCB5tdsRvoc5jl3I","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"4I16bhChGnSXpVcy","name":"Thranta","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Now an endangered species, the thranta were once a common sight in the skies of Alderaan prior to the planet’s destruction. Unlike many other flying creatures, thrantas do not use their wings as a primary source of lift. Rather, their bodies naturally produce hydrogen, which is stored in several internal air sacs that keep them aloft. This may be one reason why thrantas evolved to be creatures purely of the air, no longer needing legs on which to land. Over time, Alderaanians domesticated numerous breeds of this beast to be used as mounts. Today, only the common and baleen thrantas survive in any measurable quantity. One of the few places one can find a thranta is above the clouds on the tibanna-producing gas giants of Bespin."}},"items":[{"_id":"FJsy5thq8mnC9En7","name":"Beak","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
