{"_id":"5z84eUwjf7xb6HPd","name":"Brother Viscus","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"GeTgVrdW5KJh9i9p","name":"Enchanted staff","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"5","critical":"3","range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Defensive 1, Disorient 2, Linked 1"}},{"_id":"1JGiU7ThIN3F98MR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"48zeGizHk4RpnxUi","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"5zGGWRdKSRpzAM6x","name":"Dandy Gambler","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Force-sensitive individuals have a distinct advantage at games of strategy and chance. Some choose to become professional gamblers. As with any successful gambler, these galactic dandies never find themselves in one casino for too long, lest those who lost credits to them come looking for reparation. These lucky individuals are always on the move, searching for the next big game."}},"items":[{"_id":"UBcEEqKHfAAQuWTF","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"Dn9kIBOAaMAYWznG","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"a53pzEdCf9p8AJCC","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"60dClPtyxBqDs5cT","name":"Mechanic","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Alliance depends heavily upon a number of vehicles and starships in order to maintain their desperate struggle. In order to maintain this incredible array of technical marvels, the Alliance relies upon skilled technicians and mechanics to keep it in contention for victory in the Galactic Civil War. While many of its engineers’ Imperial counterparts have extensive military training, the Alliance tends to recruit civilians with practical experience and expertise. Commercial mechanics, personal enthusiasts, and generally anyone with a grudge against the Empire who has sufficient background is welcome to join the Alliance and serve."}},"items":[{"_id":"R9gyC9MLY2fFpORg","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"60x3Vw7WfbBjmT8a","name":"CorSec Tactical Response Team Member","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Tactical Response Team is an elite para-military unit formed form the best and brightest members of CorSec. A combination of pilot, commando, and investigator, TRT members are trained in both police and military tactics. They carry out the most dangerous missions undertaken by CorSec, such as infiltrating crime syndicates or hunting the pirates that haunt the Corellian System’s far-flung asteroid fields. Unlike the majority of CorSec, TRT members operate throughout the entire system, working closely with military and police forces from the rest of the Five Brothers as well as those aboard Centrepoint Station."}},"items":[{"_id":"kEEg4DcWBLzaFOGt","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"8MD16LAxcMGjx1m5","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"EdR7fnAkEoauZE2N","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"r2JQnbJ9xSzNit4o","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"rm397Q0wMfaEkJVU","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"perxJAsN48RUKw48","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"62AVjPpSjVIWeofD","name":"Skuir Fish","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Deep within the chilly murk of Sakiya’s oceans lurks the hideous skuir fish. A large, aggressive, sea-going predator with a sleek body and a powerful, fanned tail that carries it through the water, the skuir fish is fast and dangerous. In addition to its toothy maw, a squir fish has four long, razor-tipped appendages on the underside of its body with which it can lash out to seize its prey. All of these factors make it one of the most feared predators in the seas of Sakiya.\n\n Skuir fish average five meters in length, but they have been known to grow much larger in colder, deeper waters. Adult skuir fish are hunted for their meat by harpoon ships on Saki, but the vicious creatures claim many crewmembers of the seafaring vessels as well. Folklore even tells of a stark-white skuir fish called Oloss Yvae, which is so gigantic that it sinks entire harpoon vessels and swallows their crew whole. Many of lepatap Harbor’s albino exiles see this mythical leviathan as a symbol, a hero that exacts the revenge they desire upon their persecutors."}},"items":[{"_id":"MoMmcxZ9CpSwfw1W","name":"Razor pincers","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":5,"range":"Short","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare, Pierce 4"}},{"_id":"iN7z8h384GsSuDa4","name":"Toothy jaws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":11,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Vicious 3"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
