{"_id":"6YNqU7cSzUUJOzU8","name":"Disguise Mode","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As a maneuver, may transform into the appearance of an innocent sweeper droid. If no enemies witness the transformation, the droid immediately gains Deception 3 (:proficiency::proficiency::ability:) as a skill."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6ZiG44TryVzreUDX","name":"Dewback","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Originating from the Dune Sea on Tatooine, dewbacks are large four-legged reptiles who are well-suited to desert environments. Easily domesticated, dewbacks are used as both beasts of burden and reliable, hardy mounts, and like banthas, have been exported off-world for generations. Because of their resilience, these creatures are found in both Imperial and Alliance military forces. In the Stormtrooper Specialty Corps, sandtroopers make good use of their strengths in arid conditions; amongst the Alliance, dewbacks are deployed to SpecForce’s 4th Regiment."}},"items":[{"_id":"yVNsP0uaVMdfLldW","name":"Teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 2"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6cdhRXlH7dGuRSOP","name":"Pilot Battle Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Pilot droids of the B1 series were designed with more advanced cognitive capabilities than their infantry counterparts. In addition to basic combat and piloting protocols, the droids are programmed to maintain the ships and vehicles vehicles they utilise, whether the droids are part at a fighter wing, aboard a massive battleship, or crewing AAT-1 hover tanks. They are the standard crew of the CIS fleet and are commonly encountered by Republic troops during boarding actions."}},"items":[{"_id":"TuM2691jASB9MBJP","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6cdo3vrByakVAcLk","name":"Wol Kessix, Resistance Agent","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Wol Kessix is of medium height and unremarkable build, and trained at blending in with planetary populations across the galaxy. All his infiltration training didn’t help him when he crashed on a First Order world, however, and he is noticeably the worse for wear after his stay in the detention block. Despite his injuries, Wol handles his circumstances with a calm, knowing smile."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6e2ayTIFVblBmfWY","name":"Restraint","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Increase the difficulty of a Melee or Ranged: Light attack check by one in order to in­flict Stun damage and gain the Knockdown quality; spend :advantage: to grant this ability to a Quolas guard minion group at Short range for one round."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6eMx51dQUp9ehuWL","name":"Improvised Detonation","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per session as an action, may make a :hard: Mechanics check to build an explosive device out of available materials. The device's damage is equal to Intellect, plus Mechanics, plus :success: and possesses the Blast quality at an equal value. Spend :triumph: to increase the damage by 2. :despair: causes the device to detonate immediately."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6eqOxGZUvfsQ802c","name":"Bring it Down","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6f4piqokhNTjriot","name":"Just A Kid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When making any social checks, Boba adds :setback::setback: unless the target has a reason to take him seriously."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6fXYMrlPbbiXFVft","name":"Aggressive Negotiations","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per session as an action, may make a :hard: Lightsaber check to decrease the difficulty of all Negotiation checks the character makes for the remainder of the encounter by two to a minimum of zero."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6gIe8AjGNI9ouT19","name":"Seventh Sister","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A ruthless and power-hungry Mirialan, Seventh Sister uses the dark side of the Force to find and eliminate Force adepts. As an agent of the Inquisitorius, she also has discretionary authority to commandeer Imperial assets as required to overcome such threats. Seventh Sister is a calm and thoughtful agent, preferring finesse over brute force when in combat. She liberally uses a small team of ID9 seeker droids for reconnaissance and observation while pursuing her objectives. Their findings assist her in pursuing her foes and identifying their vulnerabilities."}},"items":[{"_id":"FcclyFE79Dong0sZ","name":"Inquisitor lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber (Agility)","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder"}},{"_id":"YceSAmAKl0JQ7IeK","name":"Inquisitor lightsaber (dual-blade)","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber (Agility)","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder, Linked 1, Unwieldy 2"}},{"_id":"9HiTwA6AxvZ4LBRX","name":"Inquisitor lightsaber (spin)","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber (Agility)","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder, Defensive 1, Deflection 1"}},{"_id":"ZpHggt05gnqBflvg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"3ta69eG5bRBkyjbQ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Ay6Axef07NT40Ojl","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"GDUwrzECBgnFnKSO","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"6JBSc40gfETpnQJf","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6gOZKkBr05M6npI0","name":"Master Starhopper","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per round, suffer 2 Strain to decrease the difficulty of a Astrogation check by 1."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6gXyICt2pvYRg4yJ","name":"Bark Rat","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The bark rat is a tree-living rodent like creature found throughout the forests and jungles of Cholganna. They often fall prey to the planet’s fearsome predators, many of which can strip a bark rat tree-nest bare within minutes. The bark rat is no easy meal, however, thanks to its thick hide, quick bursts of speed, and prehensile, whip-like tail.\n\nThe creature is covered in a thick, leathery hide that mimics the rough texture and appearance of Cholganna’s roughest tree bark. It also has a chameleon-like colour adaptation quality, making it difficult to spot when still. The bark rat is an omnivore with small ears, a flat nose, and teeth equally suited to vegetation or flesh.\n\nBark rats typically live within dead tree trunks or large branches, which they hollow out. They are not particularly perceptive; it is not uncommon for them to inadvertently remove too much material, causing a dead limb or a tree to fall, especially if a heavy predator lands on the tree. A fallen tree-nest is instantly abandoned, sending bark rats scurrying about the wilderness, eventually to regroup at a new tree. If a tree falls due to a predator, a dozen rats swarm the attacker while the others flee. Their battle tactics combine their speed and numbers. They keep on the move while their tails whip and lacerate attackers’ legs and soft underbellies. If a target falls to the ground or is wrapped around a tree limb or trunk, they swarm over it, biting and clawing at it from all sides."}},"items":[{"_id":"qyykz6XutOlZsZ4R","name":"Teeth and claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":3,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}},{"_id":"GlEy9Ckm6VlezKJy","name":"Tail","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Knockdown"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6iA8v38SLK7KzKz0","name":"Corte’s Smuggler Cew","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Tad, Vickers, Gyd, and Sira are four of Corte’s crew. A fifth crewmember, Kef, remains behind with the Titan’s Mercy, Corte’s light freighter. The four with her (two humans, a Twi’lek, and a Gand) are all young and cocky, and none of them expected any trouble as a result of this deal. Kef (the Jawa) always expects trouble, but wearily accepts that he can rarely stop his hot-blooded captain from getting in over her head.\n\nUnder the circumstances, Corte’s crewmates are surprised, but willing to fight their way out of trouble–after all, this isn’t the first time Corte’s plans have gone awry. If it looks as though the fight is going against them, they might well call out to the PCs for assistance, for they realize how dangerous Thamoss can be (despite Corte’s earlier assurances that this job would be simple and risk-free)."}},"items":[{"_id":"TFJOAYmTwsLTscjf","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6jcbg8I36iECqtvn","name":"Cheater","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As an action, during a race or chase encounter, Sebulba can make a :hard: Skulduggery check to immediately inflict 2 system strain on any vehicle in the encounter. He may do this up to three times per encounter."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6lPwWERGRYPmDPTR","name":"Kreehawk Ganger","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Jaded adrenaline junkies with a contemptuous disregard for their own safety and a burning desire to prove themselves, the young Neimoidian members of the Crimson Kreehawks gang make for dangerously unpredictable opponents."}},"items":[{"_id":"0jETQ4RAJoGJx2sn","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"rqAhSTwtOAUd6KM6","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6pa2uTpBt15zuqW5","name":"Venerable Hutt","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"By the time a Hutt reaches venerable status at over 845 years of age, its skin has tightened and shrunk on its frame, creating a hard, thick outer covering. Venerable Hutts also darken as they age, their skin tones taking on deep, dark hues. Venerable Hutts are devious, intelligent beings who will do anything to achieve their goals."}},"items":[{"_id":"OsQSoBp92lBupQiY","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"yoigtUfErp7nbEWI","name":"Large-bore laster pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":2,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"D3vG07bRrDOYsSW8","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"AccqDsN8cKYViClT","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Yhm7W4wAxMhoPkkD","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6uAlgxIp83kf6RaI","name":"CZ-Series Communications/Business Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The CZ-series communications/business droid exemplifies extreme specialisation in protocol droid manufacture. Its databanks feature a suite of languages and cultural customs smaller than comparable models, and it lacks information on species or cultures beyond the Core Worlds. Instead, the CZ-series is programmed with a near-complete database of banking and financial regulations, as well as storage space to record current market prices for any goods it might encounter. A long-range comlink enables the droid to observe markets across a whole planet or to access interstellar communications networks to track deals made throughout the galaxy. The model’s one universally reviled downside is the standard paintjob designed to draw attention to the droid in dealerships. It is a truly vulgar mix of bright green and orange – obviously, many owners have these droids repainted.\n\nAlthough the Rebellion has limited need for the business acumen the CZ-series is built for, the droids are top-notch negotiators, often capable of reaching settlements solely on the strength of their programming. Furthermore, the droid’s long-range comlink can serve as a distress beacon or homing device for Rebel cells in negotiations with groups of dubious trustworthiness."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6uTHsb8KAHRi2C25","name":"Dalyrake","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Dalyrakes are amphibious arachnids who inhabit the lakes and tidal waters of both Talus and Tralus. They stand about a meter high and are half again as long, with two flat, oval-shaped body segments, six multi-jointed walking legs tipped with wicked talons, and two crab-like pincers held well forward. The smaller, forward body segment contains their primitive ganglia, eyes, and mandibles, along with a number of long tentacles tipped with bioluminescent glands. The larger, longer rear segment contains the creature’s powerful heart and is tipped with a sharp and danger ous stinger. Strange and quite beautiful in their way, dalyrakes move with a purposeful, spidery grace.\n\nDespite their strange, occasionally frightening looks and their low intelligence, dalyrakes are easily domesticated and can be found in many homes and businesses throughout the Corellian System. While they are not affectionate, they are well-suited as pest control animals. Whether domesticated or wild, dalyrakes are slow and deliberate hunters. Typically, they submerge themselves in water or hide in bracken, underbrush, deadfalls, or piles of debris, then lure in prey with their waving tentacles. Once approached by a prey animal, a dalyrake pounces quickly and injects its target with the soporific venom produced by its stinger."}},"items":[{"_id":"Y5m2svs71hvE86z7","name":"Talons, pincers and mandibles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}},{"_id":"nAa7An3LmQGRO5QU","name":"Poisonous stinger","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":3,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 3, Prepare 1, Pierce 3"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6utg579iggaSlrSs","name":"Enduring","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Increase Soak by {ranks} (already included in profile)."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6vYQW9MYavQAtW2J","name":"Wedge Antilles","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"G0ewClfvIN3Ki87s","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"eBwK05Bxr82lPawk","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"fK5MadHizqH4ZBIX","name":"Brilliant Evasion","type":"talent","system":{"description":"Once per encounter, when piloting a vehicle or starship, may select 1 opponent and make an opposed Piloting (Planetary or Space) check. If successful, the opponent’s vehicle or starship cannot attack the character’s vehicle for 4 rounds.","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"6w6FOQGv66rHZWGF","name":"Isshtharr, Wookiee Warrior","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A towering Wookiee standing nearly 3 metres tall, Isshtharr has deep grey (almost black) fur and ornate hide armour made out of some former prey. His fur has numerous braids through it, and many ornamental trinkets dangle from those braids, representative of victorious battles and hunts.\n\nLike many of his species, Isshtharr loves combat and feels that violence solves many problems. The Wookiee is considered outgoing among his kind and tries to strike up many conversations with Rebels around the base—though most can’t understand him. He is also very inquisitive and often asks about how things work."}},"items":[{"_id":"D5wErQc6e7XWj3Sj","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"70j0b8vUOkazjt74","name":"Jedi Temple Guardian","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"During the heyday of the Republic, the Jedi Temple Guards protected the Coruscant Jedi Temple. Selected from the ranks of the Jedi by the temple’s head of security, the Temple Guards cloaked their identities behind ceremonial robes and masks. Their anonymity represented their total commitment to the ideals of the Jedi, and allowed them to serve as impartial arbitrators of conflicts within the temple.\n\nThe Temple Guardians wielded unique, double-bladed lightsabers with distinctive yellow blades. Their armour appeared purely ceremonial, but wove cunning layers of protective fabrics together to create a subtle but effective defence against blaster bolts and blades."}},"items":[{"_id":"MSBjXse2e3azh4eU","name":"Temple guard lightsaber pike","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Breach 1, Defensive 1, Linked 1, Sunder, Stun 4, Unwieldy 3"}},{"_id":"E9fIe2cuoQfYPNlN","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"itv65hK4nKdVvg87","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"TyY1vbqOaDfPfKMr","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"jprX3IZeykw9Orhx","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"715JlvSQX8G7DIAi","name":"Force Power: Unleash","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Make a Force power check targeting one enemy at Short range, roll a ranged attack as part of the pool, using :average: Discipline check instead of normal difficulty. If the check is successful and generates :darkside::darkside: the attack deals {Willpower} damage with a critical rating of 4, plus 1 additional damage per :success:. May spend :darkside: to increase damage by 3, and :darkside: to increase range to Medium."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"73upJsuKLovqVR3E","name":"All-Terrain Driver","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Does not suffer usual penalties for driving through difficult terrain when using Piloting: Planetary."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
