{"_id":"7MyJ7L0fFVdlAuCx","name":"Spir Fraxis","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Spir is a rangy young man with furtive eyes. His upper lip has been split and still bears a long lurid scar, which may explain why he seems to leer at anyone whose eye he catches. Spir has dressed up to visit the cantina in neatly tailored and close-fitting black clothing."}},"items":[{"_id":"B2u3qkS9jkuWizBS","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7NujLT2ZKu6zzI9P","name":"Auto-Fire","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Increase the difficulty of the attack by one. If the attack hits the attacker can trigger Auto-Fire with :advantage::advantage:. Auto-Fire can be triggered multiple times. Each time the attacker triggers Auto-Fire it deals an additional hit to the target."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7P78MkG5M0lbhurf","name":"Deil Kadru, Village Elder","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7VEuE3qaNfMWMQ8l","name":"Sunder (Improved)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Each :advantage: spent to activate a weapon's Sunder quality damages the item two steps instead of one."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7VpzLu3ChY0t4ELb","name":"Dimlurker","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Dimlurkers are hideous, worm-like creatures native to the dark, winding tunnels far beneath the Kystes’ Spine. One end terminates in a grasping, toothless maw, flanked by a pair of long, prehensile tentacles tipped with hard, spiked spheres of solid chitin. These lashing tentacles are the dimlurker’s primary weapons, and are used both to strangle prey and to stuff food down their gaping gullet.\n\nDimlurkers patrol the dark places beneath the Spine, eating carrion, filth, and preying on other subterranean creatures, including the Kystes’ Spine Selonians and the occasional (and unlucky) spelunker. They are completely blind and deaf, having neither eyes nor ears, and hunt by sensing heat and vibrations through the numerous clusters of receptor cells scattered throughout their bodies. In combat, they lash out with their flailing tentacles in an attempt to grab and entangle their prey. Once entangled, the prey is squeezed to death in the dimlurker’s powerful embrace and then swallowed whole."}},"items":[{"_id":"Ok8iatymxGGsCvM2","name":"Chitinous limbs","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 2, Stun 3"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7XANxNIMSAuXtAAh","name":"Serrated Edge","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Adds Vicious 1 to the weapon."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7YMIKD6rtWcl4mUA","name":"Stone Guardian","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Some facilities require discretion and art as much as they do security. Stone guardian droids are specifically designed for these situations. They provide a potent defence that is utterly in keeping with the overall tone of a site.\n\nDespite the name, stone guardians are not actually constructed out of stone. Their armoured shells are simply sculpted and painted to resemble some form of rock or marble. When inactive, stone guardians appear to be decorative statues. The statues might be freestanding, or they could appear to be a support pillar or a part of a wall. Only when they activate does their true nature become clear. A stone guardian’s passive detectors are extremely sensitive and rigged to detect any intruders who enter its domain. When they identify a threat, the droids activate and attempt to eliminate it."}},"items":[{"_id":"NZ2rbg6X2FTGTS0H","name":"Stoney fists","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Concussive 1"}},{"_id":"mxxCbMsdpFzeLVr6","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7bTfj34ahV8hUJc5","name":"Grand Inquisitor","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"It is believed that this Pau’an was once a valued member of the Jedi Temple Guard, but fell to the dark side of the Force the more he grew to believe the corruption within the Republic Senate and the Jedi Order. Under the direction of Darth Vader, the Grand Inquisitor fulfils the mandate of the Inquisitorius to find and eliminate Force-sensitive threats to the Galactic Empire. His targets include former Jedi — such as Ahsoka Tano and Kanan Jarrus — as well as children across the galaxy who have the potential to grow into threats to the Emperor. He has overseen special efforts to detect and capture young Force-sensitives such as Project Harvester at the Academy for Young Imperials on Lothal. While he uses the Spire for holding prisoners and performing interrogations, he travels freely across the Empire to find and eliminate threats personally either under orders from Darth Vader or on his own initiative and using his own intelligence leads.\n\nThe Grand Inquisitor has significant discretionary power to requisition Imperial assets, including a fleet of Star Destroyers. While he is not averse to pursuing his targets, he has a proclivity for devising traps that bring Force wielders to him. In pursuing his mandates, the Grand Inquisitor has authority over high-ranking Imperial military officers, and at times he has worked in concert with Grand Moff Tarkin."}},"items":[{"_id":"Rl3MrOZh07RZszT1","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"edSDFca9igeEnsBn","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"2bAg5RUGlwYZ3wb6","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"U1xTsvVmRvme5Fka","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"GIDjnv0q6AsnaeIg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"0FHRdGGYnaLf1oKM","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"3VZlWnklqqnPFQfE","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"wnMPg25W2W6IbMlq","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7ei2x5Y28suZ9p36","name":"Drain Life","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Whenever a shaoryn inflicts damage on a target after Soak, it heals half that many wounds (rounded up)."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7f0uKlTjbzEseB4x","name":"Prescient Shot","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7g55F5JDva3PzQ8B","name":"ISB Technician","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"4p1uiGxh9YksWkx9","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7gPotQL7k0E5vbUc","name":"Prince Sono Molec","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Sono Molec inherited control of Kowak from his father, King Atai Molec. The Prince oversees slaving operations in the southern Slice, supplying the bulk of Twi’lek, Rodian, Theelin, and Togruta slaves to both the Hutt Empire and the larger auction house on Zygerria. Sono also runs a poaching operation, supplying Kowakian monkey-lizards to buyers all over the galaxy. Since assuming control of Kowak, Prince Molec has divided slave supply worlds in the Trailing Sectors with both the Thalassian slavers and the Karazak Slavers’ Cooperative.\n\nDespite his “accomplishments” Prince Molec has never earned the respect of his father. Two years ago, Sono was touring Zygerrian holdings in the southern Slice with his older brother Hordem and recklessly got drawn into a naval engagement with Captain Nervi. The batlle ended with the defeat of the Molec forces and the death of Sono’s brother. The death of the king’s first heir drove a wedge between Sono and his father that ended in his pseudo-exile to Kowak.\n\nPrince Molec maintains a sabacc face as unreadable as ferrocrete, making him hard to read during negotiations. He leads a decadent lifestyle both personally and professionally, and he has many vices, including alcohol, gambling, and spice. Prince Molec also takes a morbid pleasure in the misery of others. However, beneath his egotistical facade, the prince is paranoid. Sono is convinced that servants within his court actively plot to depose him, which slowly chips away at his self-assured exterior."}},"items":[{"_id":"fwwtclGXdLRgJts8","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"F5IwtGVIcY12xf3w","name":"Shock whip","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Ensnare 3, Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"jslUZ2EjMxEKe0u9","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"LhjHE2D5zQNJkfQ0","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"3gsuPZq9goa9u5Kg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Kb12hdeeuXmDEG3e","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7gwzdDnbwYBI6nOr","name":"Natural Camouflage","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Any Perception checks made to detect the creature suffer :setback::setback:; this affects scanners and macrobinoculars using thermal sensors or passive light amplification as well."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7hBH0RPjYZtddyc8","name":"Rodian Lackeys","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Fondo, Tyss, and Plaado are nearly identical Rodian thugs who happily follow Toram’s every order without hesitation. They dress in heavy leather jackets, wear their weapons in low-slung holsters, and finger the blades of their combat knives threateningly whenever the opportunity presents itself."}},"items":[{"_id":"Xv81QPvwlWVG8XyU","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"DS8BtYzzKqt1FqLi","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"PMZ0oHAGx1pUtphg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7hE1eGIYnVNtclEC","name":"Master And Apprentice","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per session, may nominate one ally who has at least Force Rating 1. This ally counts their Force Rating as 1 higher until the end of the encounter."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7hwphSzt9jyJqxGU","name":"Survival","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7m9QOWhbMhhBCmKW","name":"Hoverer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When hovering the character does not have to spend additional maneuvers when navigating difficult terrain."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7mjPPjOCTRlN8laR","name":"Salerodrex","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Massive, black-eyed, single-minded killing machines, the salerodrex are the dominant predator of Selonia’s endless seas. These sleek, torpedo-shaped creatures have smooth blue-white skin with occasional grey or black mottling along their spines, and a prominent ridge of dorsal spikes. Their broad mouths are filled with a triple row of sharp, constantly growing teeth that can easily pierce the hulls of ocean-going vessels or bite a grown human in two. They have incredibly sensitive hearing and olfactory senses, and can hear the thrum of an engine or smell blood in the water dozens of kilometres away. Constantly on the prowl for food, these monsters prey on anything they can fit in their maws, but they seem to prefer live, warm-blooded creatures. "}},"items":[{"_id":"EJTd1DELgwndeP7U","name":"Teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 4, Vicious 4"}},{"_id":"LGK8eTsxLJnozq6I","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7oM2WJZtR8bz2rqT","name":"Imbue Item","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Spend a maneuver to com­mit :force: and grant one weapon at Short range +1 dam­age or decrease critical rating of weapon by one."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"7oNeKlNtuLpj8Fhr","name":"Defensive Stance","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per round on the character’s turn as a maneuver, they may suffer up to {ranks} Strain to upgrade the difficulty of all melee combat checks targeting them once per Strain spent. This lasts until the start of the character’s next turn. "}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
