{"_id":"ALDWvKuSPyLFXJGI","name":"Q-4 Borerr Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Manufactured by Quarren Industrial on the planet Mon Cala, the Q-4 borer is a diminutive cylindrical mining droid .7 meters in length and .2 meters in diameter. Moving via a repulsorlift engine, the droids use drilling lasers to burrow through dirt and soft rock in search of veins of ore, which they can detect with the use of specialized sensors. Once the Q-4 discovers ore, it continues to search for additional veins, while larger mining droids are called in to extract the discovery.\n\nReferred to as “ mole droids” by the miners who use them, Q-4s possess a cheerful demeanor and pursue their work with apparent glee. Despite their carefree and can-do attitudes, Q-4s aren’t particularly bright, and they often bite off more than they can chew if left unattended for long periods of time. They are used in small teams and deployed in large formations to search for ore, and they operated easily both in atmosphere and underwater."}},"items":[{"_id":"qlT85xBPoBl0X234","name":"Heavy-duty drilling laser","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Pierce 4"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ALN2VLRo992qxjv3","name":"501-Z Police Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"SoroSuub’s first and only foray into law enforcement droids, the 501 -Z is one of the more popular police droids currently on the market. Tall and angular, the 501-Z is clad in heavy-duty, shock-resistant armour that gives these droids a rather imposing appearance. Colloquially known as Zeds, these droids feature a sophisticated analytical droid brain that is part protocol droid and part combat droid. They are programmed for communications, community relations, riot control, and general policing, and they have a reputation as dogged and competent law enforcement officers. Some have even been upgraded to operate as detectives and special investigators, using their analytic brains and programming to great effect. While they are typically programmed to use only non-lethal force, those used by SoroSuub for corporate security operations can, and often do, use lethal force when protecting highly sensitive corporate assets."}},"items":[{"_id":"2cMAYQ5qUMS6rrqx","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"qo3qMXJACIVBE6iN","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"uu0CdgiQL671SDkp","name":"Stun baton","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":6,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Disorient 2, Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"8H83VRbWIqaG7gAD","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"33ctLGsQR7hlRF0v","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ALNMx3HGvKqLRKKq","name":"DRK-1 Probe Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These enigmatic droids are believed by the Jedi Lo have been designed according to specifications found in ancient Sith holocrons, but few have been encountered, much less recovered, providing limited basis for conjecture. Reports of these droids were first relayed by Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn during the blockade of Naboo, but more have since filtered in from isolated sites across the galaxy. Few Know who among Count Dooku’s servants has the authority to deploy the droids or knowledge of their missions. When the droids are spotted, reports are often limited or unverifiable. The Jedi and Republic Intelligence both believe the droids make use of sensor-baffling technology to become virtually undetectable to electronic equipment, and their small size and great speed make them hard to spot by unaided senses. On the rare occasions when the droids have been cornered, they typically begin firing with micro grenade launchers, attempting to either destroy then opponent or to force the opponent to destroy the droid"}},"items":[{"_id":"3z349J8h3pZXceRm","name":"Micro-grenade launcher","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Blast 4"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ALy4j7CfsCFtFutY","name":"Ewok Shaman","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"L0Zd6B8UQoEzfid1","name":"Shaman staff","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Concussive 2"}},{"_id":"0QoXttqEqfBnRhmI","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"cSWi5FH8YtrJpZCL","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AMNsozdHrcl9sYmm","name":"Knife Master","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Whenever Sugi throws her vibroknife, it gains the Accurate 2 quality."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AMaeFGh3dBudE6Ga","name":"Vornskr","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Vornskrs are lanky, canine predators native to the planet Myrkr, but found throughout the galaxy as do mesticated hunting animals, pets, and guards. They use a mild poison in their whiplike tails to stun prey, then kill it with their teeth or claws. Vornskrs are Force-sensitive, a result of hunting prey with Force-sensitivity on their homeworld. A vornskr immediately focuses on any Force-sensitive creatures or individuals in its presence as soon as it senses them, and generally attacks without hesitation. Mercenary Jedi hunters and Imperial Inquisitors have been known to use vornskrs to help ferret out Force-sensitive fugitives."}},"items":[{"_id":"VHXyHbaxiu2M6PxL","name":"Tail","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Stun 4"}},{"_id":"0HS8WDwAsR9jrXsC","name":"Teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Vicious 2"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
