{"_id":"Am5uK2M1y8pLhRtO","name":"Rathtar","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Horrifying tentacular monsters, at first glance these aliens appear to be little more than primitive eating machines, but they display complex pack hunting instincts."}},"items":[{"_id":"IyOaJ25u5lYcsTEP","name":"Plethora of tentacles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}},{"_id":"e1f0UMpvuO1a2xjX","name":"Lamprey maw","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}},{"_id":"RRTn8v0BVi4AmTHp","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"WGGqhn8b9aUvVGoR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AoqF3XsoOcTtWa2C","name":"Kindalo Guardian","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The caverns immediately beneath the Great Seal are patrolled by the zealous Kindalo Guardians, the most martial members of their species. Tasked by the loosely governing consensus to guard against any traffic between the surface and Underworld, the Kindalo Guardians depend on their great strength and extraordinary reach in physical altercations, though their eerie appearance often cows opponents into fleeing before physical confrontations can even break out.\n\nThe remit of the Guardians is to warn away or otherwise prevent any beings from the surface from penetrating the Underworld. They are likewise to prevent any denizens of the Underworld from traveling upward. Though they are exquisitely trained and prepared for their tasks, in point of fact they very rarely do anything more than stand their silent watches in the quiet of the upper caverns. Entire lengthy Kindalo generations have passed without the Guardians be ing tested in their resolve, but to doubt that resolve would be a grave error. Though relatively slow (like many humans and near-humans possessed of their great height), the Kindalo Guardians are obsessively single-minded in following the edicts that govern their ancient order."}},"items":[{"_id":"XCutOkXXOHyFaFTO","name":"Massive woody fists","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Concussive 1, Knockdown"}},{"_id":"yLg6iaru1Xznl7yv","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Aq6VDzGEGmbAw4gG","name":"Slaver","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The most abominable sort of criminal, slavers profit by robbing others of their freedom. Slavers prey upon the weak or those who cannot fight against modern technology, often locating a primitive species somewhere in the galaxy then abducting entire villages of their victims. These unfortunates can be sold off as cheap physical labor. Some advanced species are made the targets of slavery as a means of controlling a problematic population, as with the Empire’s endorsement of placing the fiercely independent and physically powerful Wookiee race into slavery."}},"items":[{"_id":"3gtYhjNseOmlWD6X","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"mWlAVDLcmIywZEos","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"YspRzK7irjY4CElA","name":"Battered stun pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":0,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Damage"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AqbVmB0As00dj5eI","name":"ISB Agent Lorn Bal","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Bal has never enjoyed his assignment on Toydaria, as Hutt domination there means he cannot wield Imperial power as fully as he would desire. Faced with the opportunity to pursue someone he believes to be associated with the mysterious mercenary under ISB scrutiny, Bal is eager to deploy his forces far from Hutt attention and to grab Dresk and anyone with him for interrogation."}},"items":[{"_id":"jJ9vo5y9SF74GLUe","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"tI56tXn4HlNTlq8C","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AqmGRa46vgOhXWmy","name":"Aayla Secura","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"KA0ExIdEeVvyKPl6","name":"Aayla’s Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"8","critical":"2","range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber (Agility)","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder, Vicious 2"}},{"_id":"SymUokSZ5KaSkkA8","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"fqxG24k4kVEwwNz1","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"IxqZjN0EAlEL95cS","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"1ezBTVQhsWKF0KLj","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"FDlMGiDYPL4OzrdZ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"acBUykNF60cLNVVR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"At7O6gufkGYhG7sz","name":"Aleena Wanderer","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The deeply spiritual Aleena often embark on quasi-spiritual journeys when the mood strikes them, traveling from village to village across Aleen. These usually elderly Aleena gather in groups of like-minded individuals to wander the stony wildernesses between the widely separated Aleena communities and homesteads. They use the isolation to observe the natural world and discuss their species’ place in the galaxy. Although many wanderers leave behind friends and family, it is not in the nature of the gregarious Aleena to cut them selves off from family permanently. The wanderers usually circle back to home and hearth at least once every year or two to check on the health and happiness of their clan members, bless any newborn children, and enjoy a few days with a roof over their heads.\n\nIn addition to their travels, these groups of wanderers often maintain the colossal statues built by earlier generations. Usually, this is a simple matter of keeping a passage way clear of debris or driving off native fauna that seek to make their dens there. However, on occasion, as in the wake of one of the not-infrequent groundquakes that plague the planet, groups of Aleena must band together to effect larger repairs, usually drawing on the resources of nearby communities. In these cases, the Aleena communities showcase their knowledge of engineering and masonry, following the directions of the travelers in righting fallen statues and repairing damaged features. Sometimes these repairs are so extensive as to constitute practical replacements of entire statues. It was these rare instances that disproved earlier theories, held by offworld xenologists, that stated the Aleena could not have been responsible for building the monuments in the first place."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AtDITXoZLfhTxWZk","name":"Amphibious","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"May breathe underwater without penalty and never suffer movement penalties for travelling through water."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"AuKYTAGNBbkQvSgb","name":"Volatile Temper","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When a social check against Queen Miraj generates :despair:, she rolls :force:. If the roll generates :darkside: then she immediately attacks the character with her shock whip. She will continue attacking the character for a number of rounds equal to :darkside: generated. She can be convinced to calm down and cease attacking early by a successful Coercion, Charm, Deception or Negotiation check from a character other than the target."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
