{"_id":"B5j6Nd6zltQcS7mJ","name":"Knytix","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"One of the most common creatures on Thyferra, the half-meter-tall knytix are docile, mantis-like insects that reside within the planet’s rainforests, easily blending in with the plant life. Vratix view the knytix as childlike genetic cousin, and often keep them as pets. The Vratix use a mixture of mud and knytix saliva to build their adobe-style treetop homes, which forms a compound that is incredibly durable and stands up to the high humidity of Thyferra’s jungle. It is also customary for Vratix, when they cause a deep offense to someone, to slaughter a pet knytix and make a soup of it for the offended party as a formal apology."}},"items":[{"_id":"lF6dw7OSPSjkyt0E","name":"Barb and teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":2,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"B69S5yrxBQD7xFMP","name":"Kybuck","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The amazingly swift kybuck is native to the Woolwarricca plains on the Wookiee homeworld of Kashyyyk. Vaguely resembling the larger tauntaun, kybucks have short tan-to-brown fur with small tails and thick horns. Unlike many other bipedal mounts, kybucks have split hoofs rather than claws or pads, which may help them reach immense speeds for a bipedal animal. Unlike most other riding animals, kybucks are not very effective beasts of burden. While they are very fast and well-trained mounts, they are only capable of carrying smaller individuals as riders."}},"items":[{"_id":"vq9AV3LxfqFfs7R4","name":"Horns","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"B6qRKZF5Uvz4OhRc","name":"Zygerrian Slaver","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Nearly every inhabitant of the Outer Rim knows of, and rightfully fears, the slavers of Zygerria. Vicious and bold, Zygerrians will stop at nothing to subjugate their prey, as their very way of life revolves around the slave trade. This dedication makes Zygerrians the most prolific slavers in the galaxy.\n\nIn combat, Zygerrian slavers usually resort to non-lethal tactics in order to maximise the number of prisoners captured. However, they are not above making examples out of rowdy prisoners in order to terrify and intimidate other slaves."}},"items":[{"_id":"OZdKo0xyOUB46EGv","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"EzXnF57Q67aH23Iz","name":"Shock whip","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Ensnare 3, Stun Damage"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"B7Wbh6VHnbB53erQ","name":"Concussive","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The target is staggered for a number of rounds equal to the weapon’s Concussive rating. A staggered target cannot perform actions."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"B8JFGctrfo8b49lK","name":"Krath War Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Though Krath war droids were generally humanoid in appearance, their unnatural movements and uncanny appearance made them a terrifying sight on the battlefield. These battle droids were designed to surprise and overwhelm their enemies in devastating shock assaults, springing towards their targets on their gyro-balanced leg assembly systems. These droids were far ahead of their time, and the Krath exiles meticulously maintained the precious few they had remaining.\n\nBuilt by Cinnagar Foundries"}},"items":[{"_id":"pmhtkziYn6xtp7oC","name":"Heavy Pulse-Wave Blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Vicious 3"}},{"_id":"MsiIXUgFpounoXkr","name":"Vibrosword","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 2, Defensive 1, Vicious 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
