{"_id":"Bk0upfewM5nW76AI","name":"Moff Dardano","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"Gj4NpniwKJiRP45A","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"6GB6rjJhtBEkwE2s","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"N8lVX3syJBT1OfnY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Bk2ofx1d8wBVmO7E","name":"Nerf","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Perhaps the most ubiquitous beasts in the galaxy, nerfs are found nearly everywhere there are humans. These cloven-hoofed, goat-like ruminants stand between 1.3 and 1.5 metres tall at the shoulder, have thick matted hair, and sport two sets of horns. They are remarkably unpleasant creatures on the whole, thanks to their stubbornness, powerful body odour, and thick, black, ropey saliva, which is extremely caustic and stains anything it touches.\n\nDocile and not easily spooked, the hardy creatures can adapt to nearly any environment, which largely makes up for their more unpleasant traits. These qualities, along with the fact that nerfs are completely unfazed by space travel, is what makes them so common throughout the galaxy. Nerfs found on Lothal are descended from ones the first colonists brought there generations ago. A number of breeds unique to Lothal have since developed, and Lothal nerfs are prized for the flavor and quality of their meat."}},"items":[{"_id":"Mzp9PL5zAEL9akh0","name":"Horns","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"BkgCCe1hPUjfn4gQ","name":"Clik","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A Verpine with a dark green and brown exoskeleton, Clik often sports coveralls and a large belt laden with tools. Clik often tinkers with and “improves” weapons to increase their output. These are not always welcome upgrades, however, and at times his enhancements can produce less than desirable outcomes."}},"items":[{"_id":"dxbK7X5izf7V7ej8","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"7SUsJbafo6gCzQq9","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Bmtnfe49mjoss4Bc","name":"Imperial Moff","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The term “moff” predates the establishment of the Galactic Republic, much less the Galactic Empire. Never has its use been more prevalent than since the Emperor co-opted it for his own use and created the position of Imperial Moff for individuals assigned to oversee an entire sector of space in the Empire’s name. Those chosen to serve as Moffs are either extremely loyal, extremely capable, or easily manipulated. Regardless, having one Imperial representative to whom other agents, such as planetary governors or system overseers, report minimizes the necessary number of personnel at the top of the hierarchy. Each Moff reports either to an Imperial advisor or, after the establishment of the Tarkin Doctrine, to a Grand Moff responsible for the governance of an oversector. Individual Moffs have incredible leeway in the organization and dispensation of resources under their command, up to and including the military assets assigned to a particular sector."}},"items":[{"_id":"TlaD50jvVC5cOr47","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"aLF521KWWRRIOF8P","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"wgRpmr75y095xVw1","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"JLBtZ1TEIZfH0ei9","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"BrOmdCTAfTMx3C6x","name":"Spaceport Urchin","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Every spaceport has at least one wretched misfit, and most have far more. A spaceport urchin is a young individual, around ten years old by human standards, that seems to have absolutely nowhere else to go and nothing else to do than loiter around the facility sticking his nose into anything that attracts his attention. Constantly underfoot, frequently annoying, and occasionally larcenous, spaceport urchins can either be the bane of visit ing spacers or welcome mascots and familiar faces. Likewise, they can either be despised by the spaceport staff or be looked upon as little brother and sisters s to be watched over. The state and disposition of spaceport urchins says a great deal about the administration and policies of a spaceport in general."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"BtlkYvQoXXZqi1gu","name":"Graayl Nor","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Graayl Nor, the leader of the bounty hunters, is a cold and calculating Barabel who has amassed an impressive twelve bounties in the past cycle alone. His group, the Red Pact, has made a name for itself, earning a reputation for getting the job done at all costs. The Red Pact includes numerous thugs and gunslingers, including a Twi’lek, a Rodian, and a Defel."}},"items":[{"_id":"xJqpSQuBt68Ku5dH","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"tkILFODJRLzJCgGy","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"wEQ9rP8i3NzbwiX1","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Bw1atuudm7DWBTwc","name":"Incom Engineer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"One of the few significant advantages that the Alliance possesses over its Imperial adversaries is in the quality of its starfighters. The Battle of Yavin demonstrated to the entire galaxy that the nature of space warfare had changed, and that individual craft of high quality, operated by highly skilled pilots, could defeat enemies of vastly larger size, firepower, and number. Until the appearance of the TIE interceptor, it was widely acknowledged even in Imperial circles that the X-wing was the premier starfighter in the galaxy. The design team of Incom, the company that developed the X-wing, had long since defected to join the Alliance. Since that time, the individual team members and their hand-selected engineers-in-training have become the most elite technical consultants the Alliance has, offering innovative advancements to the organization in a number of different arenas, but most often in the area of starship enhancement."}},"items":[{"_id":"qrkLd0CmZP0O21VK","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"uf0IaIlN6aFIgK5o","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"BwmQqGLR859Wp9dr","name":"Toydarian Royal Guard (HoBS)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"fy6JUjMvLICTHlAc","name":"Ceremonial sword","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"3","critical":"3","range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 2"}},{"_id":"pHWG6fYhcedkuQAb","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"0FTsrt3haQLVtJIP","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ByIgenC7FpDmbilc","name":"Tarvix","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The tarvix is a domesticated riding beast common through out Arbooine. This arboreal mammal has four small eyes toward the front of its squat head, although it depends more on its acute sense of smell to find its way. It has a thick coat of dark bristles, which offers some degree of protection against bearsloths and other predators. Although not particularly fast, tarvixes are tough and dependable, and just as adept at scaling trees as walking on the forest floor."}},"items":[{"_id":"MXfrt32sgdIzn3pV","name":"Claws and teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"C1F1d1x04wZokLAe","name":"Noira, Pirate Queen","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Noira is an Ubese female in her mid-forties, with pale skin and piercing blue eyes that swirl like liquid behind her platinum mask. Her hair is shoulder-length and ebony, and she wears a sharp uniform that adds even more to her air of command. As an Ubese, Noira wears a discreet breath mask that supplies her with the atmosphere mixture she requires to survive. She keeps a blaster at her side and his proficient with her vibrorapier. Her true weapon, though, is her charm. Under the circumstances, Noira is more interested in survival than combat. Things have gone poorly, and even if she survives the Consortium’s ambush, her credibility within the Veiled Sorority has been completely shattered. In fact, it’s unlikely she’ll be the Queen for much longer, and she knows it."}},"items":[{"_id":"EOFewO9X8FrOO85a","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"7jcdO6LgOFC4SwsA","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"AZVaAmqjYaJIWveF","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"ZoWF8z9QeL8GrqHH","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"P6oA4cqiyZBcuQjZ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"C37wfZzv4HGF0w9k","name":"Humming Vibrations","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As an action, may make an opposed Charm vs. Discipline check against a target at up to Medium range to disorient the target for a number of rounds equal to :success:; may spend :advantage::advantage::advantage: or :triumph: to stag­ger the target for 1 round instead."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"C5smeVsVqYS3L4FZ","name":"Droideka (Destroyer Droid)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Droidekas, greatly feared by Republic troops during the Clone Wars, were manufactured by the Colicoid species. These durable droids are capable of collapsing into a wheel like form for swift movement or unfolding into a tripodal walking gun platform protected by a powerful deflector shield. A single droideka can unleash tremendous salvos of blaster fire while remaining all but immune from return fire thanks to its shields, making droidekas more than a match for many times their own number in soldiers. Thankfully, few of these fearsome machines remain active."}},"items":[{"_id":"Qcs7A5nZw9WrcoYD","name":"Twin heavy blasters","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":12,"critical":3,"range":"Long","skill":"Gunnery","qualities":"Auto-Fire, Linked, Pierce 1, Vicious 1"}},{"_id":"qbcXODeHicYcXqQG","name":"Stomp","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Knockdown 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"C6wphnIAVEgOQilc","name":"Resistance Trooper 1","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"VsRIHg4K8ZI6XQFq","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"CQU1La331YpBi9tu","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"TNTOlUqKqgkycyyx","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"2YYIM93fLHNu7O1h","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"C8ApSRq6GfpNJvsc","name":"HK-series Assassin Droid pacifist package","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Produced by the infamous Czerka Corporation, HK-series Assassin Droids were ruthless killers programmed for unmatched lethality. Despite their sinister appearance and psychopathic behavioral programming, HK-series droids are capable of serving as protocol droids. This allows the droid a degree of plausible deniability. This protocol capability allows the HK-series droid to infiltrate by hiding in plain sight. Once in position, the droids activate their higher level assassination protocols and eliminate their targets with maximum prejudice."}},"items":[{"_id":"ygP6NoPN4ke4ATD4","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"icqvmIGQikL5zKGY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"2RVolwZQ13ozfpIl","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CA5HqdeFRTHDhx3z","name":"TC-SC Infiltration Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Produced by Cybot Galactica and marketed primarily to government and military intelligence agencies, TC-SC droids are frighteningly effective tools for espionage, infiltration, and assassination. Particularly inconspicuous-looking, they stand just under two metres tall and appears to be normal third-degree droids, such as protocol models or teaching units. They have spindly limbs, an over-sized, humanoid head with a featureless faceplate, and a set of four small, red photoreceptors. These droids come in a variety of gender programming options, and thier personalities are usually quiet and conciliatory. They seem, at first glance, to be simple, uncomplicated droids going about their drudgery with little fanfare. Which, of course, is exactly what their designers want."}},"items":[{"_id":"3C5q5tBahgccUL18","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"LQ3MyorTwFSiv8HA","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CEVMl53oFdJDb4Eo","name":"Master Pilot","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per round when piloting a vehicle using the Piloting: Space skill, suffer 2 Strain to perform any action as a maneuver instead."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CGuqh9101LyKoUaf","name":"Savrip Guards","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Queen keeps two Savrip guards, Kel and Tur, near her throne at all times. The two have been raised from birth to serve the Sorority, and they will gladly die for their Queen. The Queen uses the two Savrips to strike fear into the hearts of her subordinates and enemies. Kel and Tur wear fine, custom-made armour, and each one wields a huge spiked mace crafted from a black, nonreflective alloy."}},"items":[{"_id":"Umv0vVXlecNnUkmZ","name":"Spiked mace","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Disorient 3, Pierce 2"}},{"_id":"XYlnRK9zAklgowH3","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"jRWXfyxd0YLFdvev","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
