{"_id":"CaL1WSgGdaY2Yiqn","name":"Jakku Criminal","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Of course, where resources are scarce, there are those who would acquire them through violence and skulduggery. The criminal element of Jakku is an ever-present threat to those eking out a living day by day."}},"items":[{"_id":"5aOAvVeZAyLI7cWz","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"2i3DVpRGyUMjmmNm","name":"Duraknuckles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Caf2zio9qH1I8zza","name":"Stormtrooper: Radtrooper","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Radiation Zone Assault Troopers, or radtroopers to the common soldier, are specialist stormtroopers trained to operate in high intensity radiation environments. Armed and equipped with reinforced stormtroper armour, radiation hardened gear, and extensive training, these troopers can confidently conduct missions in even the most deadly radiation zones. To the public radtroopers provide the Empire with a capability to provide security in high radiation zones in certain planets and star systems, and to supplement local emergency responders in the event of fusion reactor meltdowns. Secretly, these troopers are often used to mop up after one of the Empire’s more heinous tactics. On worlds where the infrastructure is deemed vital to Imperial interest, but the population is considered expendable, a series of neutron bombs can be deployed to indiscriminately eliminate all life at the target. The radtroopers are sent in shortly after to root out any survivors, secure valuable infrastructure, and prepare reclamation for the Empire. Such brutal tactics are a closed guarded secret, and COMPNOR will stop at nothing to suppress the truth of these atrocities."}},"items":[{"_id":"PYEAeoqFR18EwBP9","name":"Radtrooper carbine","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"IiWVc0Nw9I66uOzH","name":"Force pike","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 2, Stun Setting"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CcRd5rorwVNjffo5","name":"Tracer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Tracer is a human Rebel agent among those searching for a new Rebel base location. She is a good fighter and a determined, dedicated agent. Although she is a bit tired and sustained minor injuries in the crash, she’s willing and able to provide the PCs with help during her own rescue. She’s a good shot and knows a thing or two about mechanics and Imperial procedure. The GM can use her to bail the PCs out of a tough spot during their escape. If the PCs have things under control, she follows their lead. If they lose their way, she jumps in to keep them moving."}},"items":[{"_id":"mJG1wOqDcGXWARju","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CfOlOOboxMNxphCd","name":"Essential Kill","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CfUi9wogbOMURKp0","name":"Roche Siak-Series Protocol Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Following the stunning failure of the J9 worker drone, the Verpine decided to redesign their protocol droid from the ground up. Roche hired a group of human contractors to assist with the new design, ensuring that the droid’s chassis and personality matrix were more appealing to a mammalian customer base.\n\nThe Siak’s personality is businesslike while remaining personable, and it can readily converse for hours about nearly any topic. Physically, the droid is a lot more human than its predecessor, while retaining some obvious Verpine characteristics. As a result, the Siak-series protocol droid represents one of Roche’s most successful products."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CgQ6KHDepThoRFq1","name":"M5-BZ","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"doGoPz3s9VVNnFmq","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"otEIELZzjnRKoHFa","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Ch7vma7DgUP8554A","name":"WSW MK-III “Harrier” Combat Remote","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"pMCF9Vh5O2FOMXHk","name":"Repeating blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":3,"range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Auto-Fire"}},{"_id":"8GkXIKPDza7Ifr7j","name":"Stun blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":3,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Damage"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Chgfn0sifNChDkBc","name":"Bloodfly Sickness","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A character who takes damage from a bloodfly bite must make an :average: Resilience check; failure results in 4 damage, ignoring Soak, and the character halves their Strain Threshold, rounding up, until the character spends at least an hour in a bacta tank or undergoes similarly extensive medical treatment (as determined by the GM)."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CjqjHCufGBFp2tqd","name":"Invigorate","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per encounter, when an ally within Short range attempts a skill check using Brawn or Agility, may roll :force:. Each :lightside: adds :success: to the target’s check; while each :darkside: adds :threat:."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ClykqzzfFKM0EZlq","name":"Gaff Kilvaari","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A veteran of the Sullustan Resistance, Gaff Kilvaari is an accomplished engineer and a talented saboteur. With a reputation as a stern but fair leader, and known for his use of overwhelming force when demolishing a target, Kilvaari makes an excellent colleague and an incredibly dangerous enemy. While generally friendly and outgoing, he is cool and reserved around members of the Alliance. While admittedly not entirely fair, Kilvaari tends to look down on Alliance operatives as either amateurs or dilettantes or both, considering his experiences in the Sullustan Resistance to have been harder and more authentic than those of the Rebels. For this assignment, he will work happily, even cordially, with the Player Characters, but only an extraordinary individual or group of Rebels can gain his trust and respect."}},"items":[{"_id":"4EVXxlGdDdaewls2","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"8MxDw2SlUViNJspP","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"FLiwIROj3bRpjPgR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"vdRNXh0QWUWwW2Yg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"S78RaUIMX9edgWb2","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"BXgLxXE1kwmT2W9P","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"fiySyaHyzfofn4JV","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"64FlcHkjkjwHAHoD","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CnQAglCBIcfZnKE8","name":"Staff Officer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The complexity of the galaxy’s conflicts mean all but the lowest level military commanders need dedicated staff officers to help plan and manage operations. Whether analyzing information, coordinating forces, planning for contingencies, or ensuring support, these officers focus on the details for their commander. This frees the commander to think big picture, able to do the art rather than the science of military operations. Thus it is said, behind every Ackbar or Thrawn are unknown, but effective staff turning their commander’s vision into reality.\n\nThe goliath Imperial war machine employs thousands of staff officers in an effort to keep the gears of war turning. Service on a staff is often seen as necessary for career progression through forging networks across branches and securing patronage from higher officers. This career climbing can come at a price for Imperial efficiency, however, as some unscrupulous officers find sabotage of others easier than succeeding on their own merits.\n\nThe Rebel Alliance, strapped for personnel at all levels, can rarely afford to spare enough officers for a full staff. Qualified officers are needed in command positions, and indeed academy trained leaders are a minority in the ranks. Instead of a rigid doctrinal definition of staff, the Alliance uses collaborative planning to perform the same basic function. Specialists from all walks of life, and all ranks, are invited to contribute when their expertise may be useful. With a galaxy-wide war of liberation to fight, most Rebel commanders will heed the words of  the former professor even if they wear a lowly enlisted rank in the Alliance’s military hierarchy."}},"items":[{"_id":"aWDPN2iG1ZtcYBbF","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"dH8FmnL11Z2A1awr","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"hF0y61L6Ubkuk9uS","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"nsBtozE5f6g2kK2B","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Cq7poZVH5rv47qRo","name":"Insight","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Perception and Discipline are career skills."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CqWx9bYegZvtajk3","name":"Vinon Scorne","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"iyzcboohs4rz3n9q","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder, Defensive 1, Deflection 1"}},{"_id":"owMt08O4qbRp8zLY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"cIVvNqr5ewPRRqFb","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"TAgeXqi2BiDjFW9Q","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"olikI3mPwaEhdIx1","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"CrPOu8eLvuOWkuRg","name":"Stormtrooper: Storm Commando Officer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Storm Commandos are the Empire’s elite fighting force, formed in direct response to the Rebellion’s guerrilla warfare tactics. Also known as shadow scouts, these troops are selected and trained to conduct special operations under demanding circumstances where regular troops prove incapable. In turn, those officers who lead storm commandos into battle are nothing less than exemplary. Only the most dedicated, skilled, and knowledgeable officers are selected to lead after undergoing grueling physical and mental tests originally instituted by the now-defector Crix Madine. Generally, Storm Commando Officers are deployed on the battlefield in one of two roles. First, and most common, is for these officers to directly lead Storm Commando groupings of 5-50 commandos on special operations. Planning and executing operations is the commando officer’s bread and butter. More rarely though, Storm Commando Officers can be deployed to mentor, and indeed lead for, other Imperial or affiliated force commanders. While not often discussed, a small team of Storm Commandos led by an experienced officer can turn even the greenest planetary defense militia into a dangerous weapon of war. These officers are supported and protected by a hand-picked team of 2-5 commandos. At the GM’s discretion, this command team can also train supported forces providing them a Boost die in Mass Combat."}},"items":[{"_id":"kpnfBWVnYoDrbynZ","name":"Blaster rifle","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":3,"range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Stun Setting, Forearm Grip, Weapon Sling"}},{"_id":"vHUAYD64zOazKmyi","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"wXoQJlacsiCrtcOj","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"2Sth31T7QIlyYsQF","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"vvy0lZevf15klmaB","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"OQcp7qRa3BUMsUDj","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Ct9xnIqW063Ep1Z7","name":"Force Power: Bind","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The character may spend :forcepip: to immobilize one target within short range until the end of the user's next turn. Spend :forcepip: to increase the range of the power by one (may activate this multiple times). Spend :forcepip::forcepip: to affect one additional target (may activate this multiple times). Spend :forcepip:; whenever an affected target takes an action, it suffers 3 Strain."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
