{"_id":"EBAWO3tvvq4YmdWj","name":"Onrein Hasa","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Onrein Hasar was once a successful executive in the Trade Federation and, once the Clone Wars broke out, an influential diplomat for the Separatist Alliance. She was one of the delegates who arrived in Jorra to negotiate a cease-fire, and was the only one to survive Warde’s assault. Although she lived, Flasar was wounded almost unto death, and the evidence of the attack is clear to this day. Scar tissue laces much of Hasar’s face, and her gray skin is gnarled from a lifetime of strife. Her glaring cybernetic eyes stare out from among the surgical grafts and cybernetic components. An implanted respirator unit projects an intimidating synthesized voice and the wheeze of cybernetic lungs. Although usually hidden beneath opulent robes reminiscent of the greatest of Trade Federation leaders, the rest of Flasar’s body features similar mechanical replacements for the flesh and bone Warde took from her.\n\nAlthough she has built a thriving criminal empire, this is the not the life Flasar had planned. To this day, she hates Warde, and it is this spite that drives her in all she does. Flasar would savor the opportunity to vent that rage on any whom she perceives as allies of Warde, whether or not they have ever actually met the fallen Jedi."}},"items":[{"_id":"eTGAd8rcc0b5KHvZ","name":"Modded blaster pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Setting, Superior"}},{"_id":"p29KXb6Vk0F66JDZ","name":"Refined cortosis staff","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Stun Setting, Cortosis, Refined Cortosis"}},{"_id":"lCGOcTMbxNOzMGnk","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"JUplM36Z8MKCb1GB","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"EBHmfHmo2CLFNqRt","name":"Field Commander (Improved)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As an action, may make an :average: Leadership check; {Presence} allies may immediately suffer 1 Strain to perform a free maneuver; spend :triumph: to allow one ally to perform an action instead."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
