{"_id":"FnPHxicXnPB7YJYR","name":"Tricky Target","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Any vehicle the character pilots counts as having a Silhoutte one lower than normal when being attacked, to a minimum of 0."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"FqU7hGX3A7bZU6hW","name":"Mehmet Alovar","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Born and raised in Coral City, the capital of watery Mon Cala, the venerable Mehmet Alovar is among the most highly respected individuals of his generation. A member of Mon Cala’s aristocracy, Alovar can trace his lineage back countless generations, to the founding of Calamari society. He has spent his long life in service to his people, first as a member of a senator’s staff, then as a senator himself, and now in his twilight years, he serves as one of the Mon Calamari peoples’ emissaries to the Alliance to Restore the Republic. A strong supporter of Mon Calamari rights and a vocal opponent of Imperial rule, he is seen by his people, and many outside observers, as a champion of free dom and peace. Despite his shining qualities, however, of which there are undeniably many, he suffers from the same short-sighted and bigoted attitudes toward the Quarren as most of his generation. In this current conflict with the Quarren, Mon Calamari officials have sent the esteemed elder statesman to negotiate a peaceful end with the Alliance, as he is guaranteed to stand firm on the Mon Calamari’s demands and protect their interests to his last breath."}},"items":[{"_id":"Dr72aI0hy5k2ip7R","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"K6UvmhF9uClvaYUh","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"srlDshQAIF0nc7WT","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"aV5nD4vEW37XqUWI","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"FWPWZBKECZuDdnPv","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"9YGpQx1MrTQvTAF3","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"FqiIvXUFVsLFkfE6","name":"Aethersprite","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"r2V4EgYUPZ73MvVX","name":"Twin medium laser cannons","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Close","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":"Linked 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Frok03oh3HILeb5X","name":"Reflect","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When struck by a ranged attack but before apply­ing Soak, suffer 3 Strain to reduce damage by {ranks|plus-2}."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"FvktGX3HciLcV1Ag","name":"Guavian Death Gang Grenadier","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Guavians are ever on the forefront of the black market weapons industry. In each of the major manufacturing houses, they have contacts proving them with “misplaced” prototypes of the most dangerous arms in the galaxy."}},"items":[{"_id":"R7sYL6XegNwRSKaI","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"Orx41X8sWAXVNoMg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"7rVVs448A47Q7V0H","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"FwKF4S1c63rsopMY","name":"Aqualish Thug","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Slightly more intelligent and more likely to use advanced technology than the Gamorrean enforcers that are popular with many crime lords, Aqualish are no less physically powerful than their porcine counterparts and equally prone to violence as a means of resolving even the mildest dispute. Although not all members of the Aqualish people are crude and thuggish, enough of them are that the sight of them acting as enforcers and henchmen for all manner of unpleasant figures is hard ly surprising to any well traveled citizen of the galaxy’s seedy underbelly."}},"items":[{"_id":"ZSDEeUbg0VoewJaz","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"kfu7rO3JdykWelT4","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"FyffCtEix5mhwfg9","name":"Chemilizard","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Also known as orpali dragons, chemilizards are native Nal Hutta reptiles that can grow to massive size. A typical adult ranges from ten to twenty meters in length and lives deep in the swamps, preying upon any creatures or beings that venture near its lair. Chemilizards have evolved the ability to extract nutrients from the planet’s polluted swamps, surviving in conditions that would kill most other creatures."}},"items":[{"_id":"uY7wMhJg0TaBAd2E","name":"Toothy bite","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 3"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"FzC5WnrL9iozvtaq","name":"Ancient Hutt Security Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These security droids date back to the time when Hutts inhabited their homeworld, Varl, and evoke the shape of their Hutt masters."}},"items":[{"_id":"Us0EMT4V9VWyGcgj","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"t7XZSUiK36rn5Roh","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"G1U2CenAIJNsEOSy","name":"Mantellian Flutterplume","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Despite their florid name, flutterplumes are one of Ord Mantell’s most dangerous scavengers. Preferring to hunt wastes and Scraplands from on high, these creatures can often be seen gliding on thermal currents in the distance in flocks of three or four. Their eyesight is quite acute, and they are always hungry."}},"items":[{"_id":"ip4oQjpaIYtFQZ4i","name":"Beak and talons","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":2,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"G1xuEVK5pgsAHhYZ","name":"New Mandalorian Cadet","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"uF31wPU47oITgRHU","name":"WESTAR-35 blaster pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"6","critical":"2","range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Accurate 1, Stun Setting"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"G2BcDSjUC5hSvyrP","name":"Quarren Agitator","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"All too often, there are occasions when diplomacy simply cannot achieve the ends the Alliance requires in order to move closer to ultimate victory against the Empire. There are many governments in the galaxy that have, either for selfish reasons or simply out of fear, allied themselves with the Empire and refuse to consider any other potential path. Most Quarren, for example, were reluctant to join the Rebellion following the liberation of their homeworld, and so many rabble-rousers stepped up to attempt to bring their people into the fold.\n\nWhen a planet’s government refuses to recognize the best interests of its people, agitators are used to reach the people themselves. Agitators are a very diverse lot, from those who possess incredible passion and charisma, to the manipulative and deceitful. Regardless of their methodology, however, it is a profession with very little room for error; having practiced, and survived, their attempts to convert their homeworld, many Quarren agitators now apply their tactics on behalf of the Rebellion in the wider galaxy."}},"items":[{"_id":"s2kJNGBMALkexjax","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"ynYPTcrLudenNnbW","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
