{"_id":"H2TOyONrLkWFd8Ct","name":"Spectre 2: Hera Syndulla","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Hera Syndulla is the daughter of Cham Syndulla, who fought for their Twi’lek homeworld of Ryloth against the Separatists, and now against the Empire in these even darker times. It was during the war that as a young girl she rescued and repaired an astromech droid known as Chopper from a crashed Republic starfighter. It was also during this time that she became fascinated with piloting. After her mother died and her father became more and more devoted to fighting only for Ryloth, Hera left to join a resistance movement against the Empire led by the secretive “Fulcrum”.\n\n Along the way Hera acquired the *Ghost*, and grew into an important Rebel commander as well as one of the best pilots around. As captain of the Spectres’ main vessel as well as de facto home for the group, she often serves as the one who settles arguments, ensures upkeep is done, and the final decider while the group is aboard."}},"items":[{"_id":"GTDGGjO7NJqLtzPc","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"BF9BxySZ0FyqIPkj","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"tg2YNGxKk5uwPMVv","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"ea7juorKuGo0cvNX","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"gcxE2ogdRs9SXnn1","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"H2pn8BaKzqQWXHwf","name":"Bad Press","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per session as an action, may make a :hard: Deception check to reduce the Wound Thresholds of an organisations members by 1, plus 1 per :success::success::success: (to a minimum of 1), until the end of the session."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"H3AGEea5I5np0j8P","name":"Dark Wolf Beastmaster","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Weequay militia-members who show an affinity with dark wolves are ushered in to a time-honored tradition through which they train and fight alongside their own raquor’daan. Great respect is given to warriors who tame wild raquor’daan, although this rarely happens. Dark wolves are believed to be the scions of the night god Raquor, and slaying a raquor’daan mother to obtain its cub is seen as sacreligious."}},"items":[{"_id":"uVgPqc0KrOBC7eDK","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"rWgVSglwZSpexqha","name":"Beastmaster’s vibro-glaive","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Defensive 2, Pierce 3"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"H4sTrQcQtEhSCz81","name":"Sarlacc","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"TjxaNLg3FaAPcgYp","name":"Tentacles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 3"}},{"_id":"01A32RJYM2OqSvWK","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Cgzi2dnBPC4gDKaO","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"H8oU0AHz7iu2QU22","name":"Rav Naaran","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Rav Naaran is a human male in his middle years. He is tall and trim, clean shaven, every inch the soldier in his black armor. Even before he engaged in true battles in the outbreak of the Clone Wars, Naaran was a master of the lightsaber and a relentless foe to pirates, criminals, and anyone else who preyed on the citizens of the Republic. His skills in battle were honed by constant fighting, and his stubborn streak was tempered by the adoption of tactical discipline. The Jedi took to his wartime position like few others in the order, and his captivity has done little to dull his expertise. In fact, his time in stasis has kept him young and vigorous beyond his true age.\n\nNaaran has remained inside the temple, concealing himself from the gatekeepers using his Force powers. He hopes to scout out his surroundings with his thralls before making a move. His power over the dark side allows him to dominate beings who have been affected by its touch, from his old victims to the corrupted icewolves of the valley. In a grim echo of his days as a Republic general, he directs their efforts from the depths of the Dawn Temple, treating the shattered stasis chambers as a command center where he can view the big picture from within the minds of his broken servants. The gatekeepers may assume he leads from the front, but in truth, he is content to bide his time until he is sure of an advantage or need for action. The gatekeepers also err in assuming that his goal is escape: Rav Naaran intends to flee, yes, but first he intends to steal all three holocrons. To do so, he must lure the temple’s champions—the PCs—out into the valley to gain himself time to overcome the temple defenses"}},"items":[{"_id":"VWPJxqMAmyMgEbYt","name":"Rav's Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Breach 1"}},{"_id":"5aJ8dSlZoURa1L1Q","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Wx88fcJITSxJv4Pj","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Z8ubJ5had8BCtbRP","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HGQsGENMt8srn7FZ","name":"Self Destruct","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As a maneuver, may transform into a ticking bomb. In this mode, the droid may not move, communicate or use its integrated blasters. As an action, it may detonate using the Self Destruct weapon profile. This instantly destroys the droid."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HHW4vwy593wv6Beh","name":"Drall Constable","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"SRjS1RENYNc1m4is","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"uPdoGWVEHgHOrFys","name":"Flash stick","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Disorient 3, Stun Damage"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HL3qrj2NQnIQW3LH","name":"Nam Beroya","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Not all Mandalorians shared the pacifistic views expressed by Duchess Satine Kryze during her rise to power on Mandalore. Nam Beroya was the Clan Awaud chieftain on Mandalore at that time. He saw no future in Satine’s great vision or of the Death Watch’s barbaric reversion to galactic conquest as part of the Shadow Collective. Beroya favoured the old ways, the path of the honourable nomadic mercenary. While Beroya’s clan fractured along factional lines, he followed his own vision and led more than three hundred like-minded Mandalorians to the snowy, evergreen forests of Vlemoth Port’s northern latitudes to live by the old ways. Over time, Beroya’s clan swelled to over eight hundred combat-ready warriors, and with the assistance of his adopted daughter, Vera, Nam Beroya led his clan on countless missions.\n\nTwo years ago, while Nam was on a hunting expedition with a local tribe of Talz, a band of Zygerrian slavers attacked, and Nam was captured defending his allies. Beroya’s clan thought he had perished in the battle, dooming him to a life of enslavement without the possibility of rescue. Prince Molec threw Beroya into his gladiatorial arena to fight for his court’s amusement, and the Mandalorian has run an undefeated streak for two years.\n\nNam Beroya is a burly, middle-aged man of Concordian descent, with olive skin covered in scars from countless battles. He possesses a cunning tactical mind and projects an air of confidence and competence that commands respect and inspires those serving under him. When leading his clan, Beroya carefully weighs every decision with care for how it would affect his people, but once he arrives at a conclusion. he charges forward like an angry reek."}},"items":[{"_id":"z8YoJsfK2q4SZQt3","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"qW3k7CpBG6Mz4hU7","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"UytHYlTr3UwIWBCR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HOyHlqmEh4zYBSEj","name":"Now This Is Podracing!","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When making Piloting (Planetary) checks, Anakin’s Agility counts as 4."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HOyhpqkLYK5e417j","name":"Warg, Savrip Guard","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Warg has served the Queen aboard her starship for as long as he can remember. THe ship’s cramped quarters used to bother him, but these days he doesn’t possess a coherent memory of anything else. Though he isn’t fond of guard duty, Warg considers himself to be very good at standing in one place for a long time. The only thing that might improve his day is something—ideally someone—to smash. Warg wears a suit of laminate armour made just for him, and he carries a massive vibro-axe that the Queen gave him as a present."}},"items":[{"_id":"8VRmbMpWuKovvLRT","name":"Massive vibro-axe","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Cumbersome 4, Pierce 2, Sunder, Vicious 3"}},{"_id":"KS2axxwIV8JMq5ZN","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"u0XWPykgMuxgRgi1","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HPFp0L0htjQ0QSUp","name":"Spectre 6: Ezra Bridger","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"In perhaps an auspicious coincidence, Ezra Bridger was born on the same day as the Empire began its life. It was that Empire that made him an orphan when it dragged his parents away for speaking out against it. Ezra grew up as a minor thief and con artist to survive. This ended when he not only aided the Spectres in a mission on his homeworld of Lothal, but revealed Force abilities to the ex-Padawan Kanan Jarrus - powers Ezra himself had no idea he possessed. Joining the crew, Ezra has since acted as spy, warrior, and missions leader for the Spectres. His skills in using the Force and wielding a lightsaber have also grown impressively under Kanan’s training. Despite this, Ezra is often irritated that he has no become more powerful and impatient to see the Empire’s thread to his friends ended once and for all.\n\nSInce joining the Spectres and later Phoenix Cell, Ezra traveled far from Lothal and encountered wonders and dangers he never imagined as a petty crook in Capital City’s back alleys. Where once he lived only for himself, he’s become a member of the *Ghost* family but also a part of the growing rebellion against the Empire. His wider experiences have also changed his goal of revenge for the deaths of his parents to that of ending the suffering and brutality it inflicts on beings everywhere. The depths of his feelings and eagerness for greater power to fight his foes more effectively, though, means he seems at many times to be just one step away from falling to the dark side."}},"items":[{"_id":"Fv2QvnlKw2wGwQHG","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"dwjWtnX1zuR2QTmC","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Breach 1, Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"glvcJapxtAglhA4S","name":"Custom lightsaber with blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"Mxdz4PCJL08TP6ib","name":"Wrist-mounted slingshot","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":5,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Disorient 3, Stun damage"}},{"_id":"0EqC3VDFyksO6Dez","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"NWtE3HnE2JM0kDcf","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"O1xLOLS7cFav4OJT","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HPofFNbPlcn0O1r7","name":"The Anvil, Arena Fighter","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Anvil, otherwise known as Parsons to his small group of what pass for friends, has been fighting in the Loaded Savrip’s arena for some time. He’s what most consider a midrate fighter who might have had a promising career if his luck wouldn’t have been so bad. Now he’s a fixture here, occasionally in a bout or who when the audience is bored or edgy."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HTfSHlnqdUHaPurg","name":"Formation Tactics (Improved)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As an action, may make an :average: Leadership to choose a number of allies within Short range equal to :success:. The difficulty of the attacks against the chosen allies are upgraded once until the end of the character’s next round. Spend :triumph: or :advantage::advantage::advantage::advantage::advantage::advantage: to have the effect last until the end of the encounter."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HTgF0z8oiTuFatbF","name":"Chameleon Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Arakyd Industries spelunker droid was originally intended for mining purposes. The Confederacy of Independent Systems modified and armed these droids for combat purposes. Removing the heavy mining gear, they added a minelayer, blasters, and a holographic cloaking array. It is the last item that led to their new name, “chameleon droids.”"}},"items":[{"_id":"4XOpDK7rJ7nnigpE","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"fSGqIuuZ8rwTe7g8","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"RzQXIzUVp52XPH1h","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"HTwityvjYzpPYBn9","name":"Utinni!","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The character removes {ranks|setback} from checks made to find or scavenge items or gear. These checks could include Negotiation, Perception, or other checks. Such skill checks take half their normal time."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
