{"_id":"I95wzst5Sasucrly","name":"Gun Crew","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"For each Imperial Gunnery Corps member in the minion group beyond the first, reduce the Cumbersome rating of their weapons by 1."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"I9O4KDYPJzO9BkHt","name":"Toydarian Agent","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Jerserra has a small group of agents of Toydaria. Its members keep a low profile due to the Hutt operations here. Led by “Boss” Trelon, the group was an almost-forgotten part of her growing power base until one of its members reported news of the auction. Immediately recognising the shard within the satue, Jerserra ordered the agents to arrange to retrieve it and kidnap its seller. Now, they hold Walisi and *Tragic Hope*, awaiting her arrival.\n\nThe GM can use the following profile as needed for Loorek, Ileon, or any of the other local Toydarians who server Jerserra on this world."}},"items":[{"_id":"2NF9HRUeURzPpzRw","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"I9gguTQAcutOYAlU","name":"Razhak","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Among the most fearsome predators on Ilum, these massive creatures are as agile as they are deadly. Averaging around eight meters in length, razhak-are armoured, segmented, wormlike creatures that propel themselves using rippling muscle ridges. Their bodies are broad and flat, covered with thick, chitinous plates in shades of white and blue. While they have no apparent eyes, their heads are topped with long, segmented antennae that serve as sensory organs. Their huge mouths feature multiple rows of serrated teeth.\n\nAggressive and solitary, razhak live in the endless tunnel systems beneath Ilum’s surface. They are deceptively fast and, when they attack, they rear up like a serpent and attempt to swallow prey whole. Anything they can’t-eat in one bite they tear into pieces by grasping it in their mouth and shaking it violently.\n\nIn addition to possessing great speed and a savage demeanour, razhak also can generate intense heat strong enough to rapidly melt solid ice and cause serious burns to exposed flesh. This ability allows them to tunnel through ice as though it were soft sand. Razhak usually build their nests inside of ice walls or densely packed snow, typically leaving the nest only to eat or mate.\n\nThankfully, while they are terrifying to behold and extremely dangerous, razhak are also easily distracted and creatures of minimal intelligence. Keeping this in mind, a clever opponent can easily outflank them, lead them into traps, or make them lose interest in attacking altogether."}},"items":[{"_id":"dRyMwTHLfR78Pxqc","name":"Mandibles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 4, Knockdown, Sunder"}},{"_id":"WujGA1YrJ8JGlFoK","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"hv7UObQjGga8GR3t","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ICpXhbxR9snU7XKX","name":"Bolstered Armour","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IEnzc15opbm0Krf6","name":"Rafe, Veteran Clone Trooper","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Jayk, Rafe and Tojo are the last remaining “rank-and-file” clone troopers in the platoon. As generalists, they are the backbone of the group, providing mobile firepower while Zeke gives orders and Oake lays down a heavy field of fire. While Jayk is the smart aleck of the group and Tojo is level-headed and stable under fire, Rafe is generally dour, pessimistic, and easily aggrevated."}},"items":[{"_id":"8LAepE4gd4AZKux7","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"AfMSbWpWLw5webAA","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"cHVxROOfnEakKLR7","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"l86CrCHvFVck6Oh0","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IJKLrbwOssnD2xtC","name":"Shadowport Mechanic","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The term “shadowport” is generally used to describe any operational starport that is free from governmental influence, be it planetary, sector, or Imperial in nature. These starports are occasionally operated by private individuals, but most often they are in the thrall of one or more criminal enterprises. Services of all sorts are available, and often high-grade technical services can be acquired. This is useful for those who wish to leave no record of their business transactions, but the cost for such discretion can be quite high. Shadowport mechanics are often highly skilled but eccentric."}},"items":[{"_id":"IpfuECGqCvPqtzku","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
