{"_id":"IRNNZxvbpRKxm59n","name":"Didn’t Forget About You","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per encounter, Tiin may upgrade the ability of a Gunnery check he makes against an undamaged vehicle or starship once."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ITLDGuceySDoNver","name":"TIE Pilot","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Commonly disparaged by the Alliance as vastly inferior to Rebellion pilots, in truth the pilots produced by the Empire’s starhghter training programs are head-and-shoulders above any other equivalent force in the galaxy, with the possible exception of the Alliance. In fact, the poor reputation TIE pilots have is no fault of their own, but rather a combination of their relatively fragile equipment (TIE fighters are known for relative fragility and weak construction) and their lack of protective amenities (shields being the most notable exclusion)."}},"items":[{"_id":"YARjdssCni1s7NGs","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IW3iENy5dJ6cOvEe","name":"R7-Series Astromech Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The R7-series is the latest member of Industrial Automaton’s highly respected R-series family of astromech droids. Designed specifically for use in the newly released E-wing multi-role starfighter, the R7-series was developed in secret, along with its bespoke starfighter, as part of a joint venture between IA and FreiTek Incorporated. Using the development of lA’s R6-series astromechs as cover, the R7 project set out to build the most competent and reliable astromech droid ever produced. Using an all-new, highly-advanced droid brain and the latest versions of lA’s tried-and-true astromech programming, the R7-series outshines even the venerable R2-series as an astrogator, technician, and starship pilot.\n\nThe R7 is an extremely novel design, using few parts or systems from earlier R-series droids. While it still has the iconic R-series barrel-shaped body, domed head, and two outboard legs with broad, treaded feet, that’s where the resemblance to its older cousins ends. The internal systems of the R7 are all new, and its power and computer systems are heavily shielded using circuit-hardening technology typically found in starfighters. The droid’s chassis is reinforced and constructed from stronger and lighter alloys than previous models. The triangle-shaped sensor eye is packed with advanced optical sensors that allow the droid to see in nearly any light as well as scan and analyze materials and structures for microfractures and stress fatigue. R7s are programmed with an eager, can-do personality that stands in stark contrast to the strange and surly personalities exhibited by their R5 predecessors.\n\nUnfortunately, despite all their advanced systems and genial personalities, the capabilities of the R7 series are limited. While they enjoy incredible synchronicity between their systems and the systems of the new E-wing starfighters for which they were designed, R7s find it difficult or even impossible to interface with older starfighters. Even the vaunted X-wing’s systems are too slow and clunky for an R7 to use fully. R7s can be programmed to interface with other starfighters, but their compatibility can never be one hundred percent. In game terms, this means that when connected with any starfighter or other vessel that isn’t an E-wing, an R7 loses the benefits of its Galaxy Mapper and Hold Together talents."}},"items":[{"_id":"VcxZOmmZRjFj47zY","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"Oq17Z0RwKLNbNxTv","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"0ZzZ2sZ1mNpV2UeJ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IWDhV5ekQ8bHeX3w","name":"Fefze Beetle","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The dominant—and principle remaining—life form on Duro’s surface, the fefze beetle is a devolved and non-sentient subspecies of the insectoid Fefze. Originally, a large swarm of Fefze was recruited to immigrate to Duro as workers. The Duros believed the Fefze would be able to handle the poisonous atmosphere and environmental damage of the mining areas; unfortunately, the toxicity levels were beyond even the Fefze, and they mutated. As the ecosystem completely collapsed and the Duros abandoned the planet, the fefze beetles were left behind to breed unchecked and scour all organic matter from the world.\n\nFefze beetles are as large as a two-person landspeeder. They are predatory by nature and attack any organic beings in their sensory range rapidly and voraciously. In addition, their digestive acids (powerful enough to break down anything remotely edible) can be spit at short ranges. The only saving grace for any group unlucky enough to encounter fefze beetles is that only a handful share a hunting area at a time."}},"items":[{"_id":"k2toJKI17Bfyk3ut","name":"Legs","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Knockdown"}},{"_id":"dR7iMmp1WdpyfRuy","name":"Mandibles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 4, Pierce 1"}},{"_id":"AdXmtHl6JDjvyIr7","name":"Acid spit","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Burn 3, Slow-Firing 4"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IX9kyTt3yPf0FfSj","name":"Fallen Apprentice","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"For every Force user who sees the myths of the ancient Jedi as an ideal to live up to, someone else decides to follow a darker path. Sometimes, these deviants seek out apprentices who will aid and emulate them. Such apprentices are often weak-willed, eager for the easy power their new master promises."}},"items":[{"_id":"JvpyCQGmWQsjJv1r","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"fxUdgnlslbG5oI0K","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"l9nDzxN4DgJ1U2wd","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"YQpd6tGdJChq3RgA","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IYGpOvnL85RypKdV","name":"Cloud-Rider Marauder","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Dreaded pirates led by the mysterious Enfys Nest, the notorious Cloud-Rider marauders are the scourge of the Outer Rim. They strike from the skies, mounted on modified swoop bikes, conducting lightning raids to snatch and grab valuable cargo. The speed of these assaults often means that by the time security forces are alerted to what is happening the marauders have already escaped. Clad in a mixture of scavenged, or looted, flight suits and local animal leathers, most marauders conceal their identities with masks or helmets. Most see the Cloud-Riders as pirates to be feared, but whispers of support can be heard in some quarters. Although fearsome in appearance and tactics, some have noticed the marauders almost always target the Imperial military or rival criminal gangs, rarely accosting innocent civilians. While the motives of the Cloud-Riders are as unknown as the true identity of their leader, the threat of a surprise attack by these marauders is well known to Imperials stationed in the Outer Rim."}},"items":[{"_id":"ntfGDUoMPgBGIIor","name":"Tibanna-jacked DH-17 blaster pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":2,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"yRs28szwQNnPv4kD","name":"Vibrobayonet","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":3,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 3"}},{"_id":"gfc5lZeg9fp6kV6u","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IYZW4tSrWV4g9JcT","name":"Bargos’s or Rebel Gamorrean","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"1DZOYO0XgUB7khcI","name":"Crude Gamorrean vibro-ax","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 2, Vicious 3"}},{"_id":"MWItAs2KfBB7y3cP","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Ic7Wzw5Y59oddiBy","name":"Shaoryn","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Shaoryn are ghostly swamp predators that haunt the southern marshes of Toydaria. They appear as a collection of wispy, yellow-white lights floating through the swamp, which has earned them the nickname “swamp pixies” among the locals. Beyond their illusions and trickery, shaoryn are tall, slender amphibians with spongy green bodies and leathery tendrils used to envelop and suck the life out of their prey."}},"items":[{"_id":"CLh6nFHF4eMd9v1n","name":"Grasping limbs","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 3"}},{"_id":"LGoG67tLFLeUgXWR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"KsGGHzGbP87jL6Zv","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"79ISScq7gQldMip2","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"IcyM2bwzEDNBeHol","name":"Q-Signal Messenger Drone","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Id68aErQlqHXCf9O","name":"Morgukai Adept","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Morgukai were comprised entirely of Kajain’sa’Nikto males, who passed down their traditions from father to son and practiced a specialized form of martial arts that made them dangerous foes, even for a Jedi Knight. The Morgukai employed an arsenal of esoteric weaponry and armour crafted with cortosis ore to make it resistant to the favored weapon of the Jedi—the lightsaber. Though they are widely thought to be extinct like the Jedi they once hunted, it is rumored that a few Morgukai persist and practice their art in secret."}},"items":[{"_id":"5Nh52LCW7nisFOKB","name":"Modded cortosis staff","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":1,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Breach 1, Cortosis, Defensive 1"}},{"_id":"PaUjWSiEFSG5gS8J","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"bEQ3V1U9Z11evm8O","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
