{"_id":"LkEKXcnOzoMvWxOd","name":"B2 Super Battle Droid (Minion)","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Created by Baktoid Combat Automata to serve as front line heavy infantry, the B2 Super Battle Droid is superior to its predecessor the B1 in all respects. Boasting reinforced armour, integrated anti-personnel weaponry, and programming capable of operation without a command signal, this hulking battle droid is a formidable foe on or off the battlefield. Before the introduction of the IG-100 MagnaGuard, B2s were seen serving as bodyguards to Separatist leaders such as Count Dooku. With the end of the Clone Wars, B2s are a rare sight. Some scavenged models serve crime lords or private militias; others have been re-purposed for use in gladiator arenas. Some abandoned B2s were never shut down, and still carry out their last orders, defending forgotten Separatist ships and installations awaiting unsuspected salvagers."}},"items":[{"_id":"v6qySscK8NrrUYpw","name":"Integrated wrist blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Cumbersome 3, Auto-Fire"}},{"_id":"c5HpgybsPDfH9m2h","name":"Rocket launcher arm","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":12,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Gunnery","qualities":"Blast 8, Limited Ammo 4"}},{"_id":"0001JeiSmoCfC55k","name":"Mechanical slam","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Knockdown"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"LmEesljpdfxn5GF4","name":"Lobot, Cyborg Bureaucrat","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A former thief with an enhanced cybernetic brain, Lobot is steadfastly loyal to Cloud City. Serving as the Computer Liaison Officer and chief aide to the Baron Administrator, Lobot is arguably the most powerful person on Cloud City. Due to the machinery in his brain, Lobot now has difficulty engaging in human conversation and very seldom speaks. When he does speak, he does not waste time on pleasantries. He is to the point and unflinchingly honest. This profile represents Lobot in his role as computer liaison officer as that is the role he is expected to fulfill in this adventure. A full profile of Lobot is beyond the scope of this adventure."}},"items":[{"_id":"VpHIJ7F32N4VPBdz","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"jZTwKS5huPtDiU9E","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"JxG7cj58gHvtr3GM","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"83wP5jZUkfN9X4rt","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
