{"_id":"TEkrTXSWeaP89am2","name":"Voralla Morbo","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As a vibrant young girl, Voralla Morbo grew up on the Isle of N’Van, a corporate retreat on Ban-Satir II within the Corporate Sector. Spending years in the service industry, working around executives from all over the galaxy, she developed a head for business and keen ears. After flitting about the galaxy with smugglers and earning a disdain for the Empire, Morbo joined the Rebel Alliance. Voralla’s unique background made her an ideal candidate to serve as an intelligence operative, and General Airen Cracken tapped her to serve as a spy and contact on Thyferra.\n\nVoralla invested in a cantina within the Zalxuc City business district. She called it M orbo’s Place, and it quickly gained a reputation as one of the finest establishments in the city. The tall, slender bartender with sultry looks and sandy blonde hair is a great conversationalist, and M orbo’s famous homemade brandy is great for loosening lips. Little do her high-class patrons know that when Voralla goes out to pick berries to make her brandy, she’s delivering regular reports back to Alliance Intelligence."}},"items":[{"_id":"zYOMuiOE5dRn3Gbg","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"TI3ocldTl2u9BqRU","name":"Butterbug Remote","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These small palm-sized remotes transmit localised information to each other and to the user. Whole batches can be linked together as a networked swarm."}},"items":[{"_id":"xk7Ev1HbxkV2EHZD","name":"Micro-tools and drills","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":2,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 2"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"TJzgc6fng6YBDS0T","name":"Jagomiri Swamp Stalker","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Jagomiri swamp stalker is a vulpine predator with coarse green fur, a fluffy double tail, and large clawed paws. The females hunt in packs while the males tend to be solitary predators. They possess a preternatural sensitivity to the Force through their whiskers, allowing them to anticipate the movement of their prey and attack before the victim can react. As its name suggests, the swamp stalker lives on the edges of marshes and other wetlands, although it has also been known to expand its hunting grounds into the foothills of the mountains of Jagomir."}},"items":[{"_id":"Xj3IsQyel0uL8Jn4","name":"Claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}},{"_id":"Qk4kimlJz3BVaxf0","name":"Bite","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 3"}},{"_id":"SOpGiDD4azMCYAKL","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"NbaLKeYquwnxVJ1T","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
