{"_id":"U5JJCYaSCVbfZJcO","name":"Yarkora Treasure Hunter","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Yarkora are a mysterious, long-lived race whose homeworld remains undiscovered by greater galactic society. Some members of their race have found their way into the seediest ports of call in the Outer Rim and use their incredibly patient methods to manipulate secrets out of even the most closely guarded individuals. These secrets they then use in the sale of information or for more profitable endeavors, the discovery of lost items and legacies to line their own coffers. Yarkora recognise the sentience of other races but do not truly consider most races to be their equal, and look upon them as lesser beings that exist only to assist them in the fulfillment of their agenda. This is not to say that they do not develop affections for others, but there is always a degree of reservation that ensures they are not fully committed to relations with outsiders."}},"items":[{"_id":"gmRQbkOWAkogMd1k","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"U7Wxn2UjUBfnMb7X","name":"Hydroid Medusa","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"9MEELTZskwi3qu3B","name":"Bio-tentacles","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"15","critical":"2","range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 2, Pierce 2, Vicious 5"}},{"_id":"FI6U2da7yGeBo3Bq","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"U8h2G1qkeC7aCVAc","name":"B2 Super Battle Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The B2 super battle droids are an improvement over the basic B1 droids in numerous ways, only their significantly increased cost keeps them from replacing their predecessors. Instead, the CIS deploys its super battle droids as the vanguard of its armies or as shock troops on advance missions into Republic territory. Small troops of super battle droids are often deployed as bodyguards for minor CIS dignitaries and officers, while a pair of them is generally viewed as sufficient to restrain any prisoner short of a Jedi. The B2 droids are nearly two metres tall and are completely covered in reinforced plating. Even their sensors are contained within the armoured chassis, leaving little in the way of vulnerability. If the droids have a clear weakness, it is in their simple combat programming. Super battle droids often focus on the elimination of targets above all else when left to their own devices, and they can easily be baited or distracted without a competent commander or tactical droid overseeing them."}},"items":[{"_id":"ICGc2RSYSGgzcqsm","name":"Integrated wrist blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Linked 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"U9NV1tg527FprllB","name":"Trusted Reputation","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As a maneuver, Bail may make an opposed Charm check against one or more characters within Short range to downgrade the difficulty of a number of future social skill checks equal to net :success: against that character once each, until the end of the encounter."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"U9PPKoTD16DJFpHx","name":"T-Series Tactical Droid (RotS)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Tactical droids are commonly found as the commanders of smaller detachments of droids and as advisers to the main leadership of the CIS droid army. The T-series models are among the most commonly fielded, ad their advanced processors are responsible for many of the Separatists’ most successful stratagems. The droids’ confidence in their own tactical prowess borders on arrogance; nevertheless, against all but the most daring or unorthodox of opponents, they can deliver victories exactly as promised, The blocky bodies of T-series droids are reasonably resistant to damage but ill-suited for direct combat compared to other droid models, especially given the extravagant cost of their processors. As such, they are rarely seen anywhere near the front lines. However, when they are involved in a conflict directly, their precise calculation of the odds of victory can embolden Separatist fighters and dishearten the Republic troops who know all too well how accurate those calculations can be."}},"items":[{"_id":"K9W0uIkdyflotuqE","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"b0DgMKMNeZaWymHJ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"020IoIDkoQVTH0bn","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"o8HMGYYxxUnizNSI","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"cGNuv6QamsSojeUR","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"U9flOD5pu3IpA9ep","name":"Admiral Trench","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"azDHGMX0TllO62i0","name":"Implanted electronet launcher","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":5,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Ensnare 5, Knockdown, Limited Ammo 1, Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"Ye0N38p7xcJWiuF3","name":"Electrocane","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Engages","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"zHrtGbDgX0LvZnmr","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"81Jf1VsJG9KW0pkx","name":"Clever Commander","type":"talent","system":{"description":"May use ranks in Knowledge (Warfare) to upgrade Mass COmbat chekcs instead of ranks in Leadership.","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"UAA8Hq38Prq3jAPH","name":"CSA Security Police","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Corporate Sector Authority is a massive corporate bureaucracy that governs a large sector of space along the Tingel Arm of the galaxy in the Outer Rim territories. The government is, as indicated by its name, a corporate entity that has complete control over the sector as a result of a unique arrangement that far predates the establishment of the Galactic Empire, but which is maintained through a mutually beneficial arrangement between those two bodies. The CSA enforces its policies and taws thr ough its taw enforcement divisi on: the Security Police. Commonty catted Espos, the CSA police are known for their brutality as well as the quality of their equipment They are much better -funded than m ost sector police forces and do n ot hesitate to crush anyone or anything that they believe threatens the peace and prosperity of the CSA’s rule over the Corporate Sector."}},"items":[{"_id":"tp4o9k2sS8BAZGP0","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"FVHjwTaryVCWZuip","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
