{"_id":"VdUtrhuRTEGSrm7Y","name":"Geonosian Valour","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"May perform a maneuver to cause all ranged attacks targeting the character to instead hit one ally or helpless enemy in Engaged range, until the beginning of the character’s next turn."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VdiYvSxqv787IIjD","name":"Brain Worms","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As an action, the Geonosian Queen may implant a brain worm into a target she is Engaged with, placing that character under her control. At the beginning of each of their subsequent turns, the target may make a :formidable: Discipline check to resist the effects. If they fail, the target remains under the Queen’s control and must follow her commands for that turn. This continues until they pass the check, the Queen is incapacitated or the brain worm is destroyed."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VgiIzjNh1t1ahKlx","name":"Glider","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Varactyls can suffer 2 strain to count as a flyer for the remainder of the turn."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Vi40Om9c5bvzLdUM","name":"Fambaa","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The enormous fambaa are have been famously domesticated by Gungans for thousands of years on Naboo, but have long been exported to many other worlds including Onderon. They are sometimes compared to the much smaller dewbacks, to which they bear some physiological similarities. Herbivorous creatures, fambaa are most often used as beasts of burden. They are also effective multi-passenger mounts, having seen combat action in the Grand Gungan Army in the decade before the Clone Wars. Despite their immense size, they are docile creatures, and are rarely phased or startled, even by the noise of battle. Gungans used them to carry immense shield generators, cannons, or armoured howdahs that could transport numerous individuals into battle."}},"items":[{"_id":"jB6z89Y5ZjIfKS3z","name":"Massive teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":12,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Breach 2, Slow-Firing"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"ViVWfB8L6wJLAIJN","name":"Crew Chief Jerion “Jolt” Terolt","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Jolt is one of Tierfon’s longest-serving crew chiefs. The extremely cheerful Sullustan mechanic is highly adept at patching together beat-up and blasted starships, particularly starfighters. Pilots like him because, instead of berating them after damaging their vessels and his work, he takes great pride in their survival and keeping their ships in space, often through highly creative methods. They soon discover that some of his unusual repairs sacrifice comfort and convenience to get the job done, and the results can go undetected by the pilots until inopportune moments during the next mission or flight. While not fatal, the repairs sometimes force the pilots to hastily alter their flying style, weapons, or defenses. Experienced pilots soon learn to take test flights after repairs or alterations, and more than a few can be heard cursing Jolt across the comm system when they discover a troublesome issue.\n\nJolt gained his nickname after he rewired the main control board of an arrogant, hateful, and disliked X-wing pilot to randomly give him irritating minor shocks every time he touched it after the first ten minutes of flight time, except when the S-foils were deployed for combat. Though nominally reprimanded by the base commander, the rest of the squadron and repair crews were highly entertained and appreciative of the lesson.\n\nJolt teaches the technique to many Rebel agents who pass through Tierfon Outpost, giving them another way to disrupt Imperial control panels on ships, vehicles, and equipment when straight-up destruction isn’t desired. In his little free time, he tinkers with other methods of clan destine technical damage and destruction."}},"items":[{"_id":"wNSs7Gusoi6TCZbz","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"65X4hi0wSyvRIHAI","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VlOVSl909u3P6hyG","name":"Canto Bight Police Officer","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The beautiful coastal city of Canto Bight is kept safe and orderly by the fine beings of the Canto Bight Police Department, or such is the outward perception. On the surface, Canto Bight police appear courteous and professional – the perfect constables. Underneath the finely tailored uniforms and polished arms and equipment, CBPD officers are more hired muscle than lawbeings. Justice is no concern to these police officers; instead they ensure the resort city’s best interests are met, whether it be brutally punishing vandals or looking the other way as to the source of laborers. Law is negotiable on Canto Bight, at least for the wealthy and connected. While there are unspoken red lines, such as anything which damages the prestige and profitability of the city’s gambling establishments, almost any transgression can be overlooked for the right price."}},"items":[{"_id":"W9YiOyhcdswQxHXI","name":"Relby K-25 blaster, Default","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun "}},{"_id":"4AVcrnoYeHbXfso9","name":"Relby K-25 blaster, Heavy","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun, Accurate"}},{"_id":"8dgUgHrcrjEZtBxi","name":"Relby K-25 blaster, Rifle","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":3,"range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Stun, Accurate"}},{"_id":"qwPALkaLvl5pPdmX","name":"Electro-shock prod","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Stun, Disorient 2"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VljW7sB8DgDuxc2I","name":"Captive Rancor","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Rancors are terrifying predators, found on worlds throughout the galaxy. Complete carnivores, an adult rancor can grow to be up to 10 meters tall. They often walk with a hunched, simian gait using their arms and hands as well as their legs. Their hands and wicked claws can be used for grasping and holding prey. Combined with their prodigious strength, a rancor can become an apex predator on most worlds it lives in. Their fearsome combat ability makes rancors popular amongst crime lords as gladiatorial opponents or “pets.” The infamous gangster Jabba the Hutt is known to keep a rancor in a cavern below his palace, and those who displease the crime lord all too often become the rancor’s next meal."}},"items":[{"_id":"iJJbsATRqrt6Gbom","name":"Massive rending claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":15,"critical":3,"range":"Short","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Knockdown, Sunder"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VoYtq5MR2VezDfnN","name":"DSD1 Dwarf Spider Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Straddling the line between a heavy battle droid and a light droid tank, dwarf spider droids are common heavy weapons platforms for the Separatist Army. These compact walkers are able to maneuver through confined spaces with relative ease thanks to the extensive articulation of their quadrupedal limb array. They are often deployed in urban combat environments and other situations that restrict the use of true tanks. Heavy armour plating covers their bodies, although it is mire limited on the droid’s underbellies, which are not normally exposed to enemy fire. The DSD1 model’s fire-power comes from a powerful, centrally mounted cannon capable of devastating long-range fire."}},"items":[{"_id":"nA4SXeNaKdzee2Nf","name":"Integrated heavy repeating blaster","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":15,"critical":2,"range":"Long","skill":"Gunnery","qualities":"Auto-Fire, Pierce 2, Vicious 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Vok0UV1QHtnRKIwC","name":"Plausible Deniability (Improved)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Remove {ranks|setback} from all Coercion and Deception checks. As an action, may make a :hard: Coercion check to convince {rank|words} uninvolved bystander NPC to leave the scene without asking questions."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VppoKwjxEzvIWTe4","name":"Cautious Smuggler","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Smuggling is a dangerous profession, requiringa mixture of luck, skill, and panache. Those smugglers with Force-sensitivity can detect a potential trap, come up with plausible cover stories for suspicious Imperial patrols, and know exactly when to dump their cargo (and when to pick it up later). Force-sensitive smugglers who get too cocky about their abilities of ten find themselves on the wrong end of the Imperial Inquisitorius, so those who realize what their sensitivity might mean keep it as quiet as possible."}},"items":[{"_id":"7ZsFhp76oTlUggi8","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"reji8KjHjuhi4mEo","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"2uYE90pWgfRtoFfQ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"PFKWJQMuM9fAp3Z2","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Vpr7Bmr7kXkjKl7c","name":"Cassie Cryar","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"RSTE7cioF97QVbrR","name":"Stunstick","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"4","critical":"-","range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Disorient 3, Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"bW0IMZQgyZJsRVsE","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"cCeaLa1tgySxenL0","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"e6zRdKkBhAfPFiYn","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"u8tz5MjQsLlO7c6f","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VqtCefXJia64NMU1","name":"Army Trooper (DoD)","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"GzLENnzI0NAebgyu","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"VZI4OYePXydAwpWl","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VrWDm580FBCSbpgG","name":"Expert Handler","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Remove {ranks|setback} from Survival checks to ride beasts."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Vug5tp6VhN9DTcJc","name":"Quartermaster","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The greatest difficulty facing the Rebellion is its lack of resources. What resources it does possess are very carefully measured and dispensed with absolute scrutiny for their purpose and intent. Some, even some among the Alliance’s ranks, look at the fleets of ships and the hidden bases that the organization commands and wonder why even minor resources like blaster packs are so rigidly controlled, but the Rebellion can survive no other way. Quartermasters, like their more formal military counterparts, are tasked with managing the Alliance’s meager resources and ensuring there is never a shortage of any essential commodity. Quartermasters are, by necessity, extremely strict and somewhat unpleasant, dealing with a never-ending stream of requests by frustrated personnel, all of whom believe that their request is, of course, completely valid. As a result, quartermasters often have a very unpleasant reputation among their fellow Alliance personnel."}},"items":[{"_id":"g9eFKRiVQPz7frIl","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"Q7qyaEqKOBUH1j22","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"J9dgQH2cmCLfeYtG","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"Vx1SZg2Kv76vSyV3","name":"Twisted Beast","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These beasts are the descendants of creatures created by ancient experiments in Sith alchemy. They possess flat, scaly faces framed by horns, but their misshapen musculature gives away their origin, as does their cruel and unnatural delight in toying with prey."}},"items":[{"_id":"Ic9RoiwrimpTym9s","name":"Vicious bite","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VxiE8m4mieCeZTZT","name":"Illo Vandin, Herglic Crime Lord","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Illo Vardin is a career gambler who made his fortune on Ord Mantell. Born on the Herglic world of Giju, he emigrated at an early age. He spent most of his formative years plying the Outer Rim’s hyperspace lanes as part of a smuggler’s crew. When the smuggler’s ship was repossessed by an angry cruie lord, Illo found himself on Ord Mantell. Like most Herglics, Illo is tall and broad, with deep grey skin. He dresses in well-made clothing that mimics fashions popular with Worlport’s gamblers, and he always wears a short cape made of black shimmersilk. He projects a calm and friendly demeanor to guests and friends, but behind this mask he is a cold, calculating, and suspicious businessman. When speaking, Illo tends to ask rhetorical questions of those around him, and is amused when individuals insist on answering them."}},"items":[{"_id":"cAbNSwm1c6Kx3ugv","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"lcH889dvVonULv2F","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"BXHKJ5jE1a5vl2mW","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"VyIKDlMEgcNfabsj","name":"Resistance Starfighter Ace","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Like the former Rebellion, whose ideals they still fight for, the Resistance puts great stock in their starfighter forces. Rightly so, for the aces of the Resistance are some of the best pilots in the galaxy."}},"items":[{"_id":"5lodyQoNV4YfzrMG","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
