{"_id":"XCcmNHSGtojrhK1j","name":"Tusken Raider Lorekeeper","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Tusken Raiders are widely regarded as unsophisticated savages, and while they do little to disabuse that notion, the Sand People of Tatooine do have a culture all their own. A Tusken Raider Chieftain may rule the tribe, but in any community the most important figure is the Lorekeeper.\n\nLorekeepers are the stewards of the history and mythology of the Tusken Raider race - memorizing the long and complex tale of their kind with perfect accuracy. An illiterate culture, without the oral tradition of these storytellers the Tusken Raiders would lose all sense of history and racial identity.\n\nPreserving their past is so important to the Sand People that reciting even a single word of the histories incorrectly is seen as a blasphemy to the race - and a crime punishable by death. As such, Lorekeppers are trained from birth to fill the role. If a Lorekeeper of a tribe dies before they are able to train an apprentice, the tribe is considered to be unworthy of existence, and quickly collapses due to infighting.\n\nDue to the perfect preservation of a long history otherwise lost or unrecorded, Tusken Raider Lorekeepers may be sought out as a valuable resource by those looking to learn more about the past of Tatooine."}},"items":[{"_id":"SdiwCTR2oL3Unhby","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"15HtfwNzJ8nb2nnO","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XEKDmE6UeCZtxdyW","name":"Insectoid Appear­ance","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"LOM-series protocol droids allow allies to remove :setback: from Nego­tiation checks or other checks made to negotiate or mediate when dealing with insectoid species."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
