{"_id":"XJvLpG6GHcEJ59vm","name":"Imperial Navy Trooper","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Often confused with the rank-and-file of the Imperial Army, much to the consternation of both groups, Naval troopers fulfill essentially the same purpose for the Imperial Navy. They are the enforcement arm that can be found on large-scale starships and naval space stations. Standard duties for naval troopers include the supervision of any and all prisoners aboard a vessel, simple guard duty, escort details for important guests, and boarding actions against enemy vessels."}},"items":[{"_id":"lX85cotim86YC5tE","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XKTPivsl802eTMrQ","name":"Canto Bight Police Sergeant","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Immaculately dressed and well spoken, the sergeants of Canto Bight’s police force represent the highly shone image Cantonica presents to the galaxy. Underneath this veneer, these non-commissioned officers understand the only true law on world is keep the wealthy clientele happy and their credits flowing. Police officers with strong records, despite a few ethics breaches, form a major recruiting pool for CBPD leadership. Many of these sergeants run their own side racket, skimming a few credits here and there. This is all but actively encouraged by higher ups, as most of these side deals depend on the continual success of Canto Bight’s luxury services. These officers do keep the peace, but will look the other way if the price is right."}},"items":[{"_id":"qU5lpqDpg0rVTAX8","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"QXIfEZqBACQkmTgR","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"mncB3KlqHMomwxy0","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"BsU4S3ksm1hJ5jz4","name":"Relby K-25 blaster, Heavy","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun, Accurate"}},{"_id":"vj6j9p54fK6UOxFX","name":"Electro-shock prod","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Stun, Disorient 2"}},{"_id":"tGVlvd1KGs9hBFKO","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XMLzhl8eGImLnjjG","name":"Weequay Sniper","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once he had won his autonomy, Ak-Mal immediately travelled to Sriluur to rescue two of his nieces before they could be enslaved. He hopes they can grow into equal partners one day, but for now they are instructed to hang back and protect Ak-Mal from a distance. Should Ak-Mal suffer too many injuries, one of the sisters attempts to rescue him while the other continues to provide protective fire from behind."}},"items":[{"_id":"kM4DjELTEMZgzxz4","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"7g3AKd8McinBkrYk","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XMkuJTK5hLDmP75V","name":"Cato Parasitti","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"ovH76uMF805tuwAn","name":"Model 38 sharpshooter’s rifle","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"8","critical":"3","range":"Extreme","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Accurate 2, Pierce 3"}},{"_id":"UpIS7peD8yXUea9n","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"EdQBo73DUos5ZQrM","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XNmAjyYOJIoz0wFU","name":"Interrogation Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The interrogation droids designed by the Imperial Department of Military Research are among the most feared weapons in the Emperor’s vast arsenal. These floating black spheres bristle with instruments of torture. Just the sight of them has been known to elicit confessions and coax out carefully guarded secrets from evem the most steadfast of prisoners."}},"items":[{"_id":"5VY8iOfjzV5x4r6R","name":"Acid jet","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":2,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Burn 2"}},{"_id":"5qZMXYK5E0qbmgpv","name":"Sonic torture device","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":0,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Concussive 3, Slow-Firing 1, Stun Damage"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XU789O9Rf0Hzc9IF","name":"Seripas (Armoured)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"DpAXhatAZBb2Ik4i","name":"Integrated repeating blasters","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"11","critical":"3","range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Auto-Fire, Cumbersome 4, Pierce 1"}},{"_id":"ob9KkhhKz69MC6h2","name":"Built-in power saw","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"7","critical":"2","range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 2, Vicious 3"}},{"_id":"HVhokmlSaBd9jRn4","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"detmRvrZHq3NS8YK","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XUJFvLr6Tyape78U","name":"Korrak","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Korraks are long, sinuous reptiles resembling a large serpent with pebbly scales and stubby legs. With eight short, powerful legs, korraks are incredibly fast and agile, and their clawed feet enable them to climb trees almost as fast as they can run. When a korrak attacks a target, it tries to wrap its long body around its prey, crushing it. The korrak’s bite also contains a potent neurotoxin."}},"items":[{"_id":"pklTZ8Y2CljFXkwZ","name":"Sinuous body","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 2, Knockdown"}},{"_id":"TFEwCpC9Nxr4ztYd","name":"Bite","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XVhWWJwytYNkmbPw","name":"Colonel Romar Kek","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Rebel Alliance places Colonel Kek in command of Defiant Core during stage three to develop the base into an efficient and well-trained operation as it takes on increasingly critical missions. It is possible that Kek’s installation could annoy the standing base commander (especially if it is a PC), but Kek has a proven track record and is respected as one of the early developers of the Yavin 4 base. Kek has a serious command style that demands respect and obedience. However, he also realises the Alliance is not a normal military organisation, and he tries to get the most out of any unusual assets or situations. When the base receives its starfighter complement, Kek is promoted to general.\n\nKek is an older human and long-time opponent of the Empire. After a while, the staff and the PCs begin to realize that Kek knows far more about the quirks and workings of a Recusant-class destroyer than he initially lets on. At first, some think he served aboard one of the Rebel-held vessels still in use, but it becomes apparent that this isn’t the case. Kek doesn’t advertise it to his command, but if confronted, he admits he is a former Separatist. He served as a gunner aboard the Recusant -class destroyer Vanguard Flare, which was destroyed in the Battle of Coruscant at the end of the Clone Wars. He escaped to another ship and made it back to Separatist space."}},"items":[{"_id":"FcXO91qJRCoYX6Ir","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"gqUtMyH0LSom9za6","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"loP2GrrNpiBfKI91","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"mQt7aAH641IFlcXB","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"YOCzqbghNwo9D0HG","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"XVpsThCsD7XzTbkH","name":"Rass","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Even the bravest of Sakiyan hunters are wise to fear and respect the mighty rass. Beneath a thick coat of long, black fur, the rass is a behemoth of pure muscle that can easily eviscerate most sentients with a single swipe of its jagged claws. Its back bristles with dozens of sharp tines that discourage attacks on the creature’s flank. Though it roams the dense forests on all fours, the rass rises to an intimidating height of four meters when it rears back on its hind legs to fight.\n\nRass nest in deforested areas where they can spot threats from far off while they blend in with the charred wood. Sakiyans see a one-on-one battle to the death with a rass as the epitome of demonstrating power and skill, and they often track the monsters back to their lairs to confront them. Traditionally, Sakiyans use the blackened bones of their first rass kill to make blade handles, and they cherish these blades as their most prized possessions."}},"items":[{"_id":"HjrU6D03w9N9I8MQ","name":"Deadly fangs","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Knockdown, Sunder"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
