{"_id":"a7JhyEHhIyJMKmtS","name":"Shyrack","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Fiercely territorial, the bat-like shyrack make their nests in the caves and tombs of Moraband in massive swarms. These blind avian predators prefer to live and hunt in dark, enclosed spaces where their echolocation grants them the advantage. Although they will defend their nests with reckless frenzy, shyracks will not normally attack any but the smallest prey. This reclusive nature is mysteriously abandoned every 63rd summer on Moraband, when shyracks spill out of their caves to fill the sky. Old Republic biologists speculated this phenomenon was the result of tectonic resonance creating powerful ultrasonic noise, and that ultrasonic emitters could frenzy or even control shyrack swarms. With the rise of the Empire, such research has been removed from all but the most remote of libraries."}},"items":[{"_id":"JsYegibmpiOofJAD","name":"Razor teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":3,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"aAkYiXBTybwvx2KV","name":"Jedi Youngling","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"1WKdnOhFqug3NXUx","name":"Training Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"6","critical":"-","range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"EuOeRyS1eDDW6cT4","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"GNvUkJJ3gLvQdNS4","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"aBX9epokQk4WwOb3","name":"Stormtrooper: Patrol Troopers","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Deployed to the Empire’s industrial and urban heartland, patrol troopers are a branch of the stormtrooper corps charged with law enforcement in areas deemed vital to Imperial interests. While local and planetary forces are left to police most of the Empire, these patrol troopers secure important shipyards, spaceports, factories, and other areas critical to the Imperial war machine. Patrol troopers are patterned after scout troopers. Flexible armour equipped with enhanced optics and real-time data uplinks allow patrol troopers to navigate urban sprawls with ease while ferreting out crime or sabotage. These uplinks all for near instantaneous information sharing of data from routine traffic information on patrol to pursuit vectors during high-speed chases."}},"items":[{"_id":"pIroMBY7LKH5Id8k","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"4bcu3jCD3ZCGDBfY","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
