{"_id":"bdF7H0Hwyb8yqAPP","name":"Pehmis Canyon Charger","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These huge quadrupeds measure nearly four metres tall at the shoulder, and their blocky construction makes them more than six metres in length from the tips of their stub-like tails to the grinding beaks with which they tear apart their prey. Their most notable feature is the massive crest emerging from their skull—a thick ridge of bone that curves forward past the flattened face of the beast and is used as its primary weapon."}},"items":[{"_id":"UiV4AX6r9Am1QDD6","name":"Ridged skull","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 4, Knockdown"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"bdMXfWQJ3jMoydlW","name":"Captain Hylo Sortuli","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Named for a millennia-old legend of the Mirialan people, Hylo left her homeworld of Mirial at a young age to seek adventure among the stars. She was a part of Cracken’s original crew during the Contruum resistance and helped Cracken steal the *Shadow Raptor*. When Cracken was promoted, she became the captain of the *Shadow Raptor*. She has a pet lizard named Bonebark that always seems inconveniently underfoot."}},"items":[{"_id":"jWhQZPBZcvUPAGwO","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"wlQI05o6UUdmtSx4","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"F7lNIZR3Z0Nn4JG8","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"bfbSZNTnHyCgOYkX","name":"The Lost","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Not all Hutts fled Varl when the world was deemed lost. Some lesser Hutts, trapped deep underground in slums, were cut off from the evacuation routes and unable to escape. These creatures devolved over the millennia and have become the Lost. Albino, feral creatures, the Lost survive in pockets of air deep underground, harassing and preying on miners working on Varl. The Lost maintain a great deal of devious cunning even as their rational minds have faded away."}},"items":[{"_id":"9c8EZvfHgvaD0YV1","name":"Claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}},{"_id":"eV7vmyu0pblnEREH","name":"Diseased bite","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Vicious 4"}},{"_id":"aGhvGT7OOykO6l2i","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"bftaPiWLQj8kNIr8","name":"Stormtrooper: Dark Trooper","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Funded and operated as a subdivision of the Imperial Stormtrooper Corps, the Dark Trooper Project was a clandestine attempt to create an even more fearsome elite fighting force which was easier to produce within a short period of time. The goal of the project was to create extremely advanced military droids that could pass for armoured humans, thus achieving the fearsome aspect required of elite military units without any concern for the environmental conditions that might limit human personnel. Although sabotaged by Alliance efforts, a small number of prototypes were completed, and the Rebellion lives in perpetual fear that the project may be continued in another, as yet unknown, area."}},"items":[{"_id":"9nnRq4arQXaMzGXw","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"H5OkDZNRb2ulMGBy","name":"Plasma shell assault cannon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":2,"range":"Long","skill":"Gunnery","qualities":"Auto-Fire, Breach 1, Concussive 1, Cumbersome 4, Inaccurate 1"}},{"_id":"vKQGyZQzBxYYqKvU","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
