{"_id":"eCGc16urdJJ4FNnL","name":"True Aim","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per round, may perform a True Aim maneuver to gain all the benefits of aiming and upgrade combat check {ranks|times}."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eCJx6YNzxK6OWBA9","name":"Dum-Series Pit Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Produced in huge numbers by Serv-O Droid, the ubiquitous DUM-series droids are a common sight in workshops, mechanics’ garages, and racing pits all across the galaxy. Introduced during the days of the Galactic Republic, these droids were constructed at the Serv-O Droid facility on Cyrillia for labour, repair and light construction use. Throughout the decades during which the DUM series has been in service, these droids have gained an unfortunate reputation as poorly programmed, hapless, and clumsy things that are often not worth the trouble of keeping. They are also highly disposable , thanks to their cheap construction and low price point; most DUM-series droids are simply destroyed or recycled when damaged rather than repaired. Scrapyards throughout the galaxy are littered with the remains of DUM-series droids, and few individuals consider them to have any worth at all."}},"items":[{"_id":"kZdVJHIgDw0h62MU","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eDDRPQdhUH052szx","name":"Patrician Lira Hardin","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A veteran with little tolerance for fools, Lira Hardin has been working on weapons of war for close to thirty years. Long before the Separatist Crisis, she left her native Gall for the Republic judicials, where she was trained as a combat engineer. She was moved to the Grand Army of the Republic for the duration of the Clone Wars, and she participated in the bombardment of Xorrn at the end of the conflict. She stayed on while the Republic became the Galactic Empire. After bearing witness to the subjugation of Rampa I, she resigned and went home to Gall.\n\nStruck by the ruin her hometown had become under Jans Coorsa’s leadership, Hardin became involved with clan politics and was quickly named patrician of the Hardin family. While she opposed Jans Coorsa at every decision, they shared a mutual respect. After the Imperial bombardment that decimated their village, Hardin convinced Coorsa to go into hiding on Xorrn. There, Hardin’s experience was invaluable in reactivating Foundry Four and creating the orbital repair yard. After Jans died, Hardin opposed his grandson, who sought higher·profile clients, particularly the Rebellion."}},"items":[{"_id":"ouvUil9frpBiRydl","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"qBBhHOv01pDTGW8t","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"F4WIbQ8xiiEe3PDp","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eEvXbopexiatkZGV","name":"Grax and Gremka","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Twin Toydarians from a village outside of Arnel, Grax and Gremka work mostly as annra farmers, but they ave made a side operation out of leading expeditions into the surrounding swamplands. Their rapid-fire negotiating style, whereby they seem to argue more with each other than actually haggle over their fees as guides, is often very effective with those unprepared for their act."}},"items":[{"_id":"wu0hf6jU2bxWU4U0","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eFH1YF3jzMHKTucs","name":"Dantris “Dani” Solomani","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"AKA Dr. Danny Solys, Jedi Mentor"}},"items":[{"_id":"ltsrF6oXOfnwJlvh","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"hCxJaGbV6fgpIx2x","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"tRIEc8Ju5rlQMP12","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"WiJ1Fbc2maqj51pw","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"pcokK2bhNrgIONdM","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"XN9H1iCNaUdtys7m","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"YC4r5SIlUd1S1stJ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eFPhqgPNlsIOoi1o","name":"Oso Maduk","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Duros prisoner is wearing a dark, dingy tunic and trousers with brown mid-calf boots. A pair of scanner goggles hangs from his neck, and he is immobilised in a stun harness. Once in hyperspace, Oso talks to anyone nearby."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eHcw7S6iYpYggcbl","name":"CN-DR, Jedi Hunter’s Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A mashup of scrap parts from Separatist salvage yards, this droid’s junky appearance hides a deadly and cruel machine. CN-DR, or “Cinder,” is a conglomeration of parts from at least a Super Tactical Droid, MagnaGuard, and a BX-series commando droid. Hidden beneath this mechanical chimera of components are high-output servomotors and a phrik armor lattice which turns the droid into a powerful combatant. While Cinder’s master engages Jedi from the further range possible, this droid is meant to fight up close. The elegance of a lightsaber has little to offer in response to a flame projector. Artumar employs his droid differently depending on the psychology of his traget. Against Jedi on the run, Cinder lies in wait to pin the fugitive with electronets or suppressible flame bursts. Artumar keeps his droid closer at hand against more aggressive Jedi, relying on the phrik-armored bulk Cinder presents as his shield. As expensive and time consuming it was for Artumar to construct Cinder, his years of working with the Separatists has hardened the Jedi Hunter against affection for droids. As such, Artumar will readily sacrifice Cinder for his own safety."}},"items":[{"_id":"OQQVFuji3l9AaAz8","name":"Flame projector","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":2,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Burn 3, Blast 8"}},{"_id":"9MtU9PCjXhMZZ98z","name":"Electronet","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":6,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Ensnare 5, Knockdown, Limited Ammo 1, Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"gboTiYOP4AnRRrOv","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Owx0HbqSVoHUJOiY","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"gBbRVg01zRbq5u74","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
