{"_id":"eNgdTS76a8kXgdKo","name":"Starfighter Ace","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The behavior of a true starfighter ace is often living verification that the common stereotype held of them by the majority of Alliance personnel is true. Many pilots who achieve the distinction of ace are hopelessly arrogant and utterly convinced of their own superiority, lending credence to such beliefs. Some wonder if this psychological profile is necessary to succeed in such an incredibly stressful, unforgiving career, but ultimately it does not matter. Starfighter aces are the darlings of the Alliance, a tremendous asset in the Galactic Civil War, and all too often, a tremendous annoyance to other members of the Rebellion."}},"items":[{"_id":"vLySamMpQ5hmxXQQ","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eQwBkx4vd8CYE6uY","name":"Trandoshan Scavenger Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Originally used for civilian applications such as search and rescue, these heavily modified drones have been refit for piracy. The ionization beam, originally used to disable malfunctioning electronics blocking rescue efforts, has been overcharged to disable shields and even cause damage to organic opponents. Their salvage drills have been upgraded with vibro components capable of savagely cutting through heavy infantry armour. With these upgrades, these so called “scav droids” serve as support to Trandoshan mercenaries in an anti-infantry role during boarding actions. The droids, equipped with repulsorlifts and stealth programming, are often dispatched ahead of the assault to disable ship defenses and terrorize the crew. When the boarding action begins in earnest the droids shift to direct support. Once a ship or structure is secured the droids turn their weapons to their original purpose and assist in salvaging any items of value."}},"items":[{"_id":"2N5lB5Wkn0b4XbOG","name":"Ionizing beam","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Ion"}},{"_id":"e263GA5M94bE52Et","name":"Scavenger drill","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Pierce 5, Vicious 2"}},{"_id":"y7gyks0Dy504FyPT","name":"Suicide Attack","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Blast 5"}},{"_id":"AgUksgYFvyXBpzik","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eUCO1ZCZY6ESX4NT","name":"Diplomatic Neutrality","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per session as an action, Dod may make a :hard: Deception check. On success, he cannot be a target of combat checks until the end of the encounter or until making a combat check."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eVbOjfmdAev7T3Rd","name":"Durable","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Subtract {ranks|multiply-10} from Critical Injury rolls made against the character."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eVzAuDb3tTifDykU","name":"Taskmaster Grint","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"An Imperial officer on Lothal, Myles Grint shares responsibility for the world’s Imperial military presence with Commandant Aresko. While much of that involves security matters, the Taskmaster’s duties focus on training cadets at the Academy for Young Imperials. Grint is devoted to the Galactic Empire, but he is also willing to abuse his authority for personal gain. Grint seems to enjoy inflicting punishment both upon the academy’s cadets and upon any citizens who do not properly demonstrate their devotion to the Empire."}},"items":[{"_id":"u4zFbaa6RDLSVF4e","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"wD0AF54SgKYdS5If","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"eYrc1FKqmknxaxJz","name":"General Grievous","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Previously a warrior of Kalee, Grievous chose to undergo the transformation into a four-armed cyborg monstrosity. Although he is not Force-sensitive, Grievous simultaneously wields several lightsabers in battle with lethal effectiveness, thanks to his skill and the strength and agility of his mechanical body. Grievous is a major force throughout the conflict, both as a strategic mind and as a battlefield nightmare. He prefers the front lines, flanked by IG-100 MagnaGuards, challenging Jedi Generals in hopes of adding their lightsabers to his collection. Between battles, Grievous rests within an isolated fortress on Vassek 3 with his pet roggwart, Gor"}},"items":[{"_id":"4vo4H1Fx4dXCYhqy","name":"4 Lightsabers","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber","qualities":"Breach 1, Linked 3, Sunder, Vicious 3"}},{"_id":"Sf8gk0bimHOSr9ZH","name":"Mechanical limbs","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 3, Knockdown"}},{"_id":"AlJ9fKTM3YdkYRjf","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"bcpjET4s29HhLgdQ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
