{"_id":"f1HNdTjWaKpOk20U","name":"Jyd Renyr, Arena Manager","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Jyd is an exceedingly portly human with a bald head and beady eyes. He dresses in a fine suit tailored for his excessive physique, and he wanders the arena’s edges with surprising speed and agility. Above all things, Jyd is concerned with profits. He doesn’t care who fights (or dies) as long as they pay the requisite charges, as well as any additional fees he decides to tack on for his trouble. Despite his lack of compassion, he’s of the opinion that anyone who wants to fight Flutterplume is either stupid or crazy."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"f2xmj5P7DF5Pje0c","name":"Demolition Droid","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"61NuL9ziNs6SdI5F","name":"Integrated twin blasters","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"9","critical":"3","range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Linked 1, Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"uYXtn0T5ixCxwXW5","name":"Self destruct","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"25","critical":"2","range":"Short","skill":"Gunnery","qualities":"Blast 15, Breach 2, Limited Ammo 1, Prepare 1"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"f2zSkWE7rKCTeydn","name":"Tetan Guard","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Tetan monarchy trains the most loyal and capable members of its system defence force for a spot on the Tetan Guard. The guards are responsible for the security of the palace and the ruling family. To a lesser extent, they protect the entire royal bloodline and that of any Tetan noble. As warriors, they are fearless when defending their leadership, and as investigators they are tireless at seeking justice for those who threaten the security of the Tetan elite."}},"items":[{"_id":"SLSgelJzwn0Vxnqh","name":"Ceremonial rifle","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":3,"range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"1kSEYtqfT8t50kfU","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"f53MRT3gJvYJUjuU","name":"Loth-Cat","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Members of the far-flung tooka family, loth-cats are small, wild felines native to Lothal. They are, on average, about a metre long and can weigh as much as fifteen kilograms. They have short, brindled coats with white bellies; long, thick tails; and narrow, black legs that end in long, sharp claws. Their faces are remarkably expressive, with solid black eyes, large ears, and a broad mouth full of needle-sharp teeth.\n\nLoth-cats live solitary lives primarily in Lothal’s vast grasslands, coming together only to breed and raise kits. Hunting by sight and hearing, they prey largely on loth-rats and other assorted rodents and avifauna. Expert stalkers, loth-cats hunt their prey for hours or even days, waiting for the perfect time to attack. Once committed, a loth-cat springs from hiding and attempts to kill its prey as quickly as possible. When attacking prey larger than themselves, usually when frightened or cornered, a loth-cat typically goes for a target’s face first, clawing at eyes and any other sensitive areas. Loth-cats only fight larger prey until they can escape or the creature is driven off, and will run if they can.\n\nWhile most are wild, loth-cats can be domesticated, with varying degrees of success. They make fine, if capricious and slightly destructive, pets. With enough patience, they can even be trained to hunt and retrieve."}},"items":[{"_id":"2HZAogf1kbPFL8V7","name":"Teeth and claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 2, Knockdown"}},{"_id":"LfBOZ4lvo7OeEOHf","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"f67kkNxU5y8Q550D","name":"Skilled Slicer","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When making a Computers check, may spend :triumph: to gain some measure of control over the target system. Further Computers checks within this system can be made as maneuvers."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
