{"_id":"hCBjDWq0dUyvCTae","name":"Gundark","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Native to the planet Vanqor in the Outer Rim Territories, the gundark is one of the most ferocious and aggressive species in the known galaxy. Semi-intelligent, gundarks grasp the basic use of tools, but they lack any known language or other hallmark of a sentient species. Their sheer ferocity has made them a popular target for big game hunters and those who enjoy pitting creatures against one another in gladiatorial-style contests. In this way, the beast has spread to different worlds throughout the galaxy, where it flourishes in certain environments and planets. In many cases, the beasts are hunted to extinction because of the threat they pose to natural wildlife and the denizens of a given planet, but on worlds with larger regions of untamed wilderness, packs of gundarks can survive and thrive in areas without ever encountering sentient life."}},"items":[{"_id":"fHjLoXsga88dfyWl","name":"Meaty fists","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":8,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 1, Knockdown"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
