{"_id":"lNjAa3GhiqgFJiL3","name":"Guilded Bounty Hunter","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"By definition, a bounty hunter is an individual in possession of an Imperial Peace-Keeping Certificate who is legally permitted to hunt and apprehend wanted criminals in exchange for bounties offered by the Empire or other parties. The definition is somewhat innocuous, however, and does little to reflect the sheer brutality so often exhibited by bounty hunters throughout the galaxy. Compassionate souls are not drawn to this line of work, and while many make a good living working for the Empire, just as many, if not more, choose instead to work for corporations, private citizens, or criminal organizations in order to gain the credits and the reputation that they so desperately crave. It goes without saying that bounty hunters are a persistent, significant threat to the safety of all members of the Rebel Alliance."}},"items":[{"_id":"Jn3F8C6BoTsMqvO1","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"omemqjkSBugTqRUo","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"K0ys9x3VaPAMMsYB","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"AMQlEmTMsuxAlRuW","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Ep1lGXKP30KUkK2i","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"lQ7tSuhnLxlI7c5Q","name":"Force Manifestation","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These ghastly forms are embodiments of Trech’s guilt over the crash brought to life through his Force abilities, of which he is unaware. Each manifestation is a uniquely horrid representation of his fixation on his feelings of guilt."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"lQGkjfp5zQsFDXRK","name":"Great Ibbot","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The largest living species of avifauna on Drall, the great ibbot is a majestic and imposing bird with a high animal intelligence and a fierce demeanour. These gigantic birds stand three to four metres tall on average and have a wingspan of over ten metres. Their plumage is similar to the flame ibbot, primarily copper- or brass-coloured with black and brown highlights, with white or cream-coloured feathers on their abdomen and the undersides of their wings. Great ibbots have wicked, serrated orange beaks that can slice through nearly any material as if it were rotten cloth, and powerful talons that can tear a gundark limb from limb. They feed primarily on fish and other aquatic life-forms, and are particular to spikefish, snatching the massive creatures from lakes and seas when they surface for air. Although they prefer fish, wild specimens have a tendency to prey on herd animals (and even domesticated pets, on occasion).\n\nDue to their size and relative intelligence, great ibbots are easily domesticated. They take training quite well and can follow complicated multi-step instructions. The Wingriders, Drall’s state police force cum courier service, are mounted on these great beings and are the most visible keeper of great ibbots. There are also a number of tour companies who offer adventure tours of Drall’s countryside mounted on great ibbots, although these are rare due to the danger of mounting untrained individuals on willful, intelligent giant raptors."}},"items":[{"_id":"SlPFHSPFNHtZaFN7","name":"Sharp beak and slashing claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":10,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 3, Sunder"}},{"_id":"cQJf0PsF7FGDM7Ky","name":"Stoop","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":12,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Concussive 2, Knockdown, Prepare 1, Vicious 2"}},{"_id":"g7tQK4Jog2XhRnQc","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"DejKWALV1qxiw8jD","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"lQOOgF9lHG5F9y5b","name":"Zerala Dinn","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Zerala Dinn is a longtime associate of Blaise Zirkonn and an exceedingly cunning intelligence agent. A human male hailing from Naboo, Dinn was once a thief and con artist operating in the Mid Rim and Outer Rim. Blessed with an abundance of luck, a devious nature, and a connection to the Force, he made his living forging documents and selling counterfeit art and artefacts to museums.\n\nA few years ago, he had a run-in with Zirkonn that, luckily for Dinn, ended favorably for both parties. Finding that they had much in common, including their Force sensitivity and a predilection for hurting people, they struck a partnership that would bring them both surprising amounts of wealth and influence.\n\nDinn is currently operating on Naboo under orders from the Inquisitorius. He is Zirkonn’s agent in Theed, posing as a dealer in rare antiquities and helping her find Force users. Their current ploy of leading naive would-be Jedi to their doom with the promise of ancient Jedi artifacts is working surprisingly well. They have already captured a dozen individuals who show promise as Force adepts, and they are constantly on the lookout for more."}},"items":[{"_id":"VNXOMJVeNGl3uT2A","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"8LwDYWGjp4gUXpal","name":"Refined cortosis gauntlets","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Cortosis"}},{"_id":"muTTflKICWi4utVy","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"KoRyUowsL1Dvgeub","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"wNGMFZLPM3zxVGTb","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"GhgaB2nogJUJ5JkM","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
