{"_id":"lRzlJ1H2n89EnhcA","name":"Pantoran Guardsman","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"KFGOW43EqmVrYmsp","name":"Pantoran ceremonial sword","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"4","critical":"2","range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Defensive 1, Pierce 2"}},{"_id":"jWeaHQHNyU2cqX5W","name":"Pantoran ceremonial rifle","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"7","critical":"3","range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"P6vHYIZ5Udry4I8A","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"lSXwgnaXZRAO7JLf","name":"Kad Solus","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A respected member of the Mandalorian camp at Arumorut and the second in command to Vera, the camp’s leader, Kad is a young, lanky human warrior in blue-and-green armour. Kad was born into bondage, enslaved by Nok, a Thalassian slaver expanding his business on Tatooine. A number of years later, a local crime lord hired some of the Mandalorian mercenaries at Arumorut to eliminate Nok’s operation. During the attack, Kad. at only five years of age, warned the Mandalorians before Nok could spring a trap. After the battle, a Mandalorian named Avin Solus adopted Kad and raised him as his own.\n\nNow, though still young Kad is already a battle-hardened veteran and jaded beyond his years. When the blaster bolts start flying, he often sits back at first, finding the weak point in the enemy’s strategy. Once the enemy notices him, he charges and attacks like a man expecting to die. His allies struggle to see the genius in his tactics, and call him *mir’shupla*, or “brain damaged,” despite how often he rescues them."}},"items":[{"_id":"OedMTIJdQlms0Hpe","name":"GALAR-15 blaster carbine","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":9,"critical":2,"range":"Long","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Accurate 1, Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"HRbhiFEA6SCONzIE","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"lT9AKCQcczKI7TqL","name":"Imperial Army “Mudtrooper” Swamp Trooper","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Imperial Army swamp troopers served as the army infantry’s combat specialists in wetlands environments. While all but phased out in favor of stormtroopers by the height of the Rebellion, these army troopers were relied upon to subjugate Imperial worlds during the first decades of the Empire. Equipped with partial armour, filtration systems, and survival gear, these troopers faced treacherous and disease-ridden environments nearly as deadly as their opponents. Fighting in these brutal conditions earned swamp troopers the moniker of “mudtrooper” after hellish battles on worlds such as Mimban.\n\nSwamp trooper duty was notoriously miserable. Few volunteered, with many in the ranks conscripted from planetary defense forces. Some were wash outs from the officer, stormtrooper, and starfighter corps. Others were army enlistees, signed on for a single term of service to gain skills or pay for university, unlucky enough to be assigned as swamp troopers. Whatever the source, mudtroopers were known as an unpredictably motley crew with unpredictable levels of discipline. Imperial high command often mitigated this by assigning mudtroopers to the first wave, with more reliable stormtroopers assigned as insurance against insubordination or cowardice."}},"items":[{"_id":"tOpX3AXKmFw48gr6","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"s4pJjd0InflRHvzS","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
