{"_id":"pWrzx4VisGS5jvJ2","name":"Guf Drolg","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Huge, dim-witted, and evil tempered, guf drolgs are perhaps the most disruptive and despised creatures on Talus. Roughly the size of a large speeder truck (and half as intelligent), guf drolgs are massive, quadrupedal, reptilian herbivores who make their homes on the broad grassy Talusian plains. The guf drolg’s powerful frame is draped in thick, rust-coloured hide which falls about it in loose folds, protecting it from both the elements and predators.\n\nGuf drolg herds of thousands are constantly on the move, migrating across the planet with the seasons and devouring everything in sight. Great migrations of guf drolgs cause incredible damage to local economies and ecosystems as they consume crops, destroy fences and buildings, trample livestock, and ruin the land with their acidic droppings. While they are difficult to hunt and roundly despised, guf drolgs do have some value, mostly as a source of food and hides. Their meat is surprisingly delicious, and their thick, supple hides are easy to work with, take dyes easily, and are used to make everything from armoured clothing to designer shoes."}},"items":[{"_id":"fbSxr7JVyHBnfsJK","name":"Goring horn","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 3, Prepare 1, Vicious 1"}},{"_id":"x8ZEUtXtbkZEo827","name":"Trample","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 3, Inaccurate 1"}},{"_id":"igWRkt3nErn8CqOQ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"pWxpHUWuAf8CFBxs","name":"Raider Warlord","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The warlords who roam the Madlands tend to be as cunning and vicious as they are insane. They rule their warbands through fear, and the promise of plunder and wealth for those who follow. Some of the most dangerous warlords even are said to be able to call upon fell magics to destroy their enemies with a gesture."}},"items":[{"_id":"c9JMnNDFabJQceUF","name":"Viper-blade reaper","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Linked 1, Pierce 2, Vicious 2"}},{"_id":"eo4XBronSMGGrsyC","name":"Light thrower","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Innacurate 1, Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"c0rWmp8s2xCnYM1V","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"mbxUrEuoQQ4mZDbb","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"TQuVUcKfog31ruVP","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
