{"_id":"pn68LCfnPVrQ7zzy","name":"Gyrowheel 1.42.08-Series Recycling Droid","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A relatively common sight aboard colony ships and in the streets and alleys of countless settlements, Veril Line Systems’ Gyrowheel series recycling droid is, in its way, perhaps the most useful and important droid a colony can possess. Using a powerful cocktail of natural and artificial enzymes contained within their bodies, these droids turn garbage, food scraps, and other organic refuse into a nourishing nutrient sludge that can make up the large part of many a colonist’s daily caloric intake.\n\nStanding around two metres high, these had working droids consist of a broad, round body like a high-walled serving platter around 2.5 metres across covered by a retractable clamshell cover. Dexterous manipulator arms ring the droid’s body, and a dull red photoreceptor constantly scans its surroundings for trash. The droid’s body is perched on a single hard rubber wheel and is kept balanced by a sophisticated gyro-stabilisation system. More a remote than an actual sentient droid, these extremely dim-witted constructs are devoid of individual personality beyond a desire to hunt trash. They operate in packs, scouring their surroundings for organic refuse under the command of a central monitoring computer system."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"poAbqIK8SEjg0DJ4","name":"Mandalorian Warrior","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Every sentient being born in Arumorut begins training in combat at a very young age. While many choose one specific skill to specialise in, all Mandalorians at Arumorut pride themselves on their combat prowess. It is common for younger warriors to constantly seek new challenges and ways to test their skills."}},"items":[{"_id":"Hsju5oppSkpANzr6","name":"Armoured gauntlet","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":4,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient 3, Knockdown"}},{"_id":"zOyYr109CzbpTjVq","name":"GHOVOR-22 Blaster pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":4,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun Setting"}},{"_id":"qaiK1jGGacSndcXF","name":"Mythosaur axe","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":2,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Melee","qualities":"Cortosis, Pierce 3, Vicious 3"}},{"_id":"WReKAwrDQyXGQrmJ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"poJARwlKB5Wdf8Ru","name":"Blessing of the Ancients","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per game session as an incidental, the elder may have a character within Short range heal 4 wounds."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"pskdm2klIuBh1cJR","name":"Urtuaa Haaot, Ithorian Diplomat","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Urtuaa is a two-metre-tall Ithorian with pale brown skin. He dresses in earth-toned robes and usually wears a satchel over his shoulder containing various diplomatic communiques. The Ithorian can be a bit scattered and dishevelled at times, with numerous papers and documents spilling from his satchel and hands.\n\nThe Ithorian is a calm individual who doesn’t anger easily. Urtuaa has a deep hatred of the Empire and news of their atrocities and subjugation of worlds raises his ire. He is welcoming to new Alliance members and quick to help any who need his assistance."}},"items":[{"_id":"YsLlWXcwvy0orpXO","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"JBizaMYFcgdFNBJh","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"pxsO3Pj7RKzFLLNJ","name":"Neurotoxin Doses","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Imperial assassin has multiple doses of neurotoxin, which can be introduced into food or drink, or applied to a Melee weapon as a maneuver; if applied to a weapon, it lasts for the remainder of the encounter; if a target ingests poisoned food or drink, or suffers wounds from a poisoned Melee weapon, the target must make an :average: Resilience check; if failed, the target suffers 5 Wounds, plus 1 Strain per :threat:; :despair: means the target must test against the poison again at the start of the next turn."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"pzRKPOmfrIKNhtxa","name":"Imperial Gunnery Corps","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The Gunnery Corps is a subdivision of the Imperial military that includes members of both the Imperial Army and the Imperial Navy—although there are more of the latter than the former. As with troops in the Vehicle Corps, with whom they often work, members of the Gunnery Corps receive rudimentary training as troopers, but the bulk of their instruction is in the use of vehicle- or installation-mounted weaponry. The ubiquitous turbolasers that are found on the hundreds of different starships in use in the Imperial Navy, as well as the vast variety of lasers that are deployed in ground installations and the many vehicles employed by the Vehicle Corps, are all fired by members of the Gunnery Corps."}},"items":[{"_id":"ceI3LpQ8qREe2H61","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"ZpM0AWTecefxPvZb","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"q2r97b8eNaLqvOWq","name":"Asharl Panther","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Asharl panthers are one of the more common predators on Ilum. They are large, aggressive, territorial felines that make their homes in Ilum’s high northern and southern latitudes. Adult asharl panthers average between two and three metres long and stand roughly one metre high at the shoulder. Their four powerful legs end in two-toed feet equipped with nonretractable claws. The creatures’ bodies are covered in dense, smooth fur in shades of white, grey, and blue that holds their body heat in to protect them from the cold and driving wind. They have broad, earless heads with pronounced brow ridges, and their faces are remarkably expressive, with short, blunt snouts and golden eyes. The most noticeable feature is a pair of long, tentacle-like sensory organs that grow from their shoulders. Asharl panthers live in small family groups and typically hunt in pairs or in groups of four."}},"items":[{"_id":"z4o21N6wdPwCwNFc","name":"Teeth and Claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":5,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Pierce 2"}},{"_id":"zOuWudFFsnJuYv21","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"q3A55f42Q61xN9m3","name":"Con Artist","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The charismatic, smooth-talking con artist is the subject of many a holodrama, but in reality, those who live by the art of the grift would rather not be noticed at all. The cons they run range from simple games of chance on a street corner to elaborate schemes involving dozens of operatives, deft disguises, and false credentials. However, the goal is always the same–swindle as many credits as possible, preferably with the marks never realising they’ve been conned."}},"items":[{"_id":"xUYbIGgU3JbWL2Wu","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"Wwl6PO4AAfggva1o","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"61Sraievsqqs1v5e","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"q3bgVf5HaeaeITLG","name":"Knowledgeable Healing","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When the character performs a successful Medicine check, may spend one Destiny point heal {Knowledge: Xenology} additional Wounds."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"q778B17mGTKygroj","name":"Wise Warrior","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Once per round when making a combat check as an incidental, may spend one Destiny point to use any characteristic for the check."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"q7zVPxCsatuydZ7h","name":"AP-5","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"A prickly RA-7 series protocol droid with masculine programming, AP-5 was a navigator and military analyst for the Republic Navy during the Clone Wars. He supported several deployments and served at the Battle of Ryloth. When the Galactic Empire came to power, it deemed AP-5 obsolete and reassigned him to a bulk freight as quartermaster. Many years after the Clone Wars, a now depressed and irritable AP-5 befriended fellow Clone Wars veteran Chopper, Phoenix Cell’s astromech droid.\n\nAfter some convincing, AP-5 accepted Chopper’s invitation to join Phoenix Cell. Finally fulfilling his primary programming again, AP-5’s cross-referenced Imperial, Republic, and Lasat astrogation charts to determine a safe haven for Phoenix Cell, deciding on Atollon. His brave actions saved Chopper’s friends, and as a result, AP-5 was given the role as Chopper Base’s quartermaster where his logistical expertise helps bring order to the often chaotic supply situation at the base. He also provides Commander Sato with intelligence analysis. While AP-5 has never felt better, his gratitude expresses itself as dry insults and biting sarcasm."}},"items":[{"_id":"qjSiaHxzRcaqBWQp","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"lFhWOXvOcLCCP257","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"Meqyy7FitDyBBd2H","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
