{"_id":"ts3RhlHk87IBjwED","name":"Depa Billaba","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":""}},"items":[{"_id":"zwkIyqN4eY25D9O8","name":"Depa’s Lightsaber","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":"9","critical":"2","range":"Engaged","skill":"Lightsaber (Willpower)","qualities":"Breach 1, Sunder"}},{"_id":"mJufKF7cJNkkRkku","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"mSjxIMhiUX7dO6Kb","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"CfPPI8TjtMwdThCh","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"CDtTzXhZ2NH5gWFC","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"QRW66QsQqEk9foNs","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"gV5nUYhy3pqnDooE","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"g9hOsPfoQgREjkXV","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"tvMYlDDB7lYGJwSc","name":"Ryale Wei, Majordomo","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Ryale Wei has ably served the Veiled Sorority for most of her life. Though she’s always aspired to assume the role of Pirate Queen eventually, she takes some comfort in being a lotal second-in-command. She firmly believes that most of the Queen’s decisions are actually hers anyway, and she enjoys taking credit for the Queen’s actions. Ryale is a female human in her middle years, with platinum hair and golden eyes. She’s vain to a fault, and has used regenerative treatments to maintain her youthful appearance for many years now. Aside from her extreme vanity, she’s also overconfident. Even if confronted with violence, Ryale doesn’t fight back. She prefers to guarantee her safety through surrender and delaying tactics."}},"items":[{"_id":"Lr0IoqaQcR1bPG44","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"9Q3XERfGCSlokYbQ","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"lpvEcQw39NUXLyEc","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"twIalatiOqXAAQ4B","name":"Major General Billek Vilneon","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Combined Arms Steamroller\n\nIn the eyes of Major General Vilneon, the Imperial Army is a machine. A trained engineer, experienced armoured officer, and decorated commander, it should be no surprise a man who has spent more than half his life working with war machines sees the military in this way. The Imperial Army is a complicated with a vast array of specialties, unit types, equipment loadouts, and tactical procedures. Infighting between the branches and the use of pet projects to advance careers further divides the Army. Little enrages Vilneon more than this, for he sees it as akin to debating whether the repulsorlift or the powerplant is more important on a hovertank – both are vital and must work in concert. General Vilneon has thus made a career of organizing combined arms groups from different branches and service, building true teams with strong cohesion and identity. While fully implementing Imperial doctrine and uniformity, Vilneon has added something the Imperial military lacks despite its stated ideology: unity.\n\n7th Assault Battlegroup\n\nBattlegroups are normally commanded by High Colonels, with Major Generals commanding a Corps comprised of several Battlegroups. Given General Vilneon’s high status, it should be no surprise the 7th Assault Battlegroup has a unique task organization. A normal Assault Battlegroup would be composed of two line regiments, an assault regiment, and an armoured regiment. The 7th instead has two assault regiments augmented with walkers, an armoured regiment, and a stormtrooper regiment. These troops train extensively in combined arms operations. Retaining the regimental system for little more than administrative purposes, this battlegroup is functionally organized around a series of combined arms brigades that train and fight together. The result is a highly coordinated, and therefore deadly, opponent to face on the battlefield."}},"items":[{"_id":"zDWDWkVwSIlPjaRD","name":"Blaster pistol","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":7,"critical":3,"range":"Medium","skill":"Ranged: Light","qualities":"Stun"}},{"_id":"0RLSnfXdfMOSounm","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"LzWdTXzlSuH1ZANr","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"dRo8H6wYAT8wjBBj","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"txgNenboD8UG7D1B","name":"Stormtrooper: Sandtrooper","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Desert worlds are often rich in minerals or other infrequently appearing resources, necessitating settlement despite the harshness of their environments. The extreme temperatures, as well as the abrasiveness and navigational problems associated with the terrain, necessitate specialized training and equipment. Sandtroopers are intimately familiar with arid environments, and are trained in beast-riding as a means of enduring transportation under conditions that might otherwise cripple conventional forms of technology."}},"items":[{"_id":"FYYCOXuZAGhsaeSL","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"PA4I7R4qdQEPUzFY","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"u2UVe8Xlz7P08kiT","name":"Ysalamir","type":"minion","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Ysalamiri evolved on Myrkr, where one of their chief predators was the Force-sensitive, Force-detecting vornskr. As a result, ysalamiri developed an unusual defense: a natural “bubble” around them that negates other creatures’ ability to influence the Force. These docile, tree-dwelling creatures resemble half-meter-long furred lizards and live deep within the forests of Myrkr, where they have claimed the canopy as their own. They are herbivores, feasting on the sap of the trees in which they live, and they use only their teeth to defend themselves if attacked. As a result of their Force-negating abilities, ysalamiri are highly valued as pets and companions by anyone who fears those who use the Force."}},"items":[{"_id":"rdwSxjrUPRQ5sDwC","name":"Teeth","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":1,"critical":5,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":""}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
