{"_id":"ulvEXXHCeKzR9cQQ","name":"Maalraa","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"The maalraa is a non-sentient, feline pack hunter that uses the Force to cloak itself from its prey. Although once found through out the galaxy and sometimes domesticated as guard animals, maalraas are now extremely rare, found only in a handful of the galaxy’s forgotten places and in the seediest corners of the criminal underworld. The maalraa’s ability to cloak itself makes it almost impossible to spot among the shadows, although those who are sensitive to the Force can sometimes detect its presence. When it strikes, the maalraa uses its huge fangs to latch onto its prey and hold it inert, slowly crushing it, while other members of the pack finish the unfortunate creature."}},"items":[{"_id":"symGfIynn1EYcdt3","name":"Fangs","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Ensnare 2"}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"um6Esz9JOuR6SVZ5","name":"Military Informant","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"These individuals (or, as the Empire refers to them, intelligence assets) are a pale reflection of the agents from the Imperial Intelligence Bureau. However, they are equally loyal and enjoy the benehts of deep, virtually impenetrable cover. Suitable candidates are selected at a very early age and discreetly indoctrinated when there is a reasonable explanation for their absence. These individuals are instilled with great loyalty to the Imperial military complex in exchange for extremely meager rewards in the grand scheme of things, whether they are military, monetary, or political in nature. These men and women are given legitimate civilian reasons to be moved t o political hotspots, where they carefully monitor the population for any signs of treason or paramilitary activity. They then dutifully report this information using blind drops, encrypted communiques, or other secretive means."}},"items":[{"_id":"dj2dX6AAdcQkpIlS","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"wpB1fX7tEpGAs3C8","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"upF2iWOSa0IKTyBn","name":"Cunning Ambusher","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Opponents add {ranks|setback} to Initiative checks using Vigilance."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"uqP8XAYqQSEFX5oZ","name":"Regeneration (Durge)","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"When recovering from wounds via natural rest or in a bacta tank, recover 1 additional Wound. First-aid, medical treatment, and stimpacks do not result in recovery from an additional wound. Durge can regrow lost limbs."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"urTBwpCGgtv5b7JX","name":"Once a Learner","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"As an action, may suffer 4 Strain to increase the Force rating of one ally within Short range by {Force Rating} until the end of the end of the character's next turn."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"usUNBo9zvZLH2dNT","name":"Trandoshan Slaver","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Resolute and ferocious, Trandoshan slavers are among the vilest groups in the entire underworld. While they specialise in the slavery of WooKiees, they rarely refuse the opportunity to put their combat prowess to the test. No matter whether the prey is a creature or a sentient being, a Trandoshan lives for the thrill of the hunt."}},"items":[{"_id":"iMdnXsoE5LHnKgK2","name":"Weapon","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":0,"critical":0,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Ranged-Light","qualities":""}},{"_id":"6Ewckg0H3OhCT78l","name":"Accelerated charged particle array gun","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":6,"critical":3,"range":"Short","skill":"Ranged: Heavy","qualities":"Blast 5, Stun Damage"}},{"_id":"xo5tN82CRXOL6gon","name":"Claws","type":"weapon","system":{"damage":4,"critical":3,"range":"Engaged","skill":"Brawl","qualities":"Disorient, Knockdown"}},{"_id":"ieYSseu37Rn5RRXN","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}},{"_id":"b2VT8zTP0WGQ1CY6","name":"Talent","type":"talent","system":{"description":"","activation":"Passive","tier":1,"ranked":false}}],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
{"_id":"utlKpvDfqqJLWQp4","name":"Creature of Illusion","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"characteristics":{"brawn":{"value":2},"agility":{"value":2},"intellect":{"value":2},"cunning":{"value":2},"willpower":{"value":2},"presence":{"value":2}},"stats":{"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"strain":{"value":0,"max":10},"soak":{"value":0},"defence":{"melee":0,"ranged":0}},"biography":{"description":"Combat checks targeting Moraband Sith phantasms always use Willpower in place of the characteristic normally associated with that skill; the Pierce and Breach qualities do not reduce a Sith phantasm’s soak."}},"items":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0}}
